{"id":"beats-535dad","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"BACKLOG"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T07:00:01.722045Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-f2947b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"split rendering for parent-child issues","description":"## Description\n\nTwo rendering strategies based on tab:\n\n### All Issues tab (flat + breadcrumbs)\n- Child issues with a different status from parent render as standalone rows\n- Prefix with breadcrumb: `Parent Title \u003e Child Title` (or parent icon + ID)\n- No tree nesting, no parent duplication\n- Child issues with same status as parent still nest normally\n\n### Active/Backlog tabs (tree with parent duplication)\n- Parent issue appears in each status group where its children exist\n- Children group under their parent within the same status section\n- Parent row in non-home groups shows as a lighter/ghost row (it's a reference, not the primary)\n- If multiple children share a status different from parent, parent appears once in that group with all those children nested\n\n## Notes\n- This matches the standard approach\n- The All Issues tab is the simpler view for scanning everything\n- The Active/Backlog tabs preserve the hierarchical context","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-21T07:34:13.649443Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-f2947b","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T07:34:47.78678Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
