{"id":"beats-49c21a","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-d5eacaa8-0523-4bdb-b78c-0ec115e1138d","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded a label distribution card to the Dashboard. Implemented as part of the broader Dashboard polish pass alongside [[beats-12c9f8]] and [[beats-0be7ab]] — all three breakdowns now sit side-by-side in a single row sharing a `DistributionSection` helper.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- `web/src/components/Dashboard/Dashboard.tsx` — extracted a reusable `DistributionSection` component (title + Active/All filter toggle + Card with rows). Computes label counts on the filtered issue set (Active = non-DONE by default), sorts by count descending, bars scale to the max count in the set.\n- Each row: `LabelBadge` on the left (label colors preserved), monochrome `text-secondary` bar (kept neutral so the colored badge does the visual work), count + percentage right-aligned with tabular nums.\n- Empty states distinguish \"no issues\" from \"no labels on filtered issues\".\n\n## Note\n\nThe three composition cards are slated to be demoted into a collapsible \"Composition\" section in a Phase 4 follow-up issue once the new story-led Dashboard layout (pulse / attention / epics / workload) lands.\n\n## Verification\n\n`make frontend` builds cleanly. Manually tested filter, sort order, color rendering against bg-tertiary."},"created_at":"2026-05-26T11:53:28.700699711Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-12c9f8","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-a8e43431-a045-4dc3-960d-4de8e235fd50","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded a by-assignee breakdown card to the Dashboard. Sits in the same single-row `DistributionSection` group as [[beats-49c21a]] and [[beats-0be7ab]].\n\n## Implementation\n\n- `web/src/components/Dashboard/Dashboard.tsx` — computes counts per `issue.assignee` on the filtered set. Issues with no assignee are aggregated into a single \"Unassigned\" row rendered at the bottom in italic muted text.\n- Row label: `Avatar size=\"xs\"` + display name (email stripped via `split(' \u003c')[0]`, truncated for long names).\n- Sorted by count descending (Unassigned always last).\n\n## Verification\n\n`make frontend` builds cleanly. Manually tested with mixed assigned/unassigned issues."},"created_at":"2026-05-26T11:53:37.605974709Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-0be7ab","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-025ae0f3-cd03-4f60-a4b1-9562858b7205","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded a by-priority breakdown card to the Dashboard. Sits in the same single-row `DistributionSection` group as [[beats-49c21a]] and [[beats-12c9f8]].\n\n## Implementation\n\n- `web/src/components/Dashboard/Dashboard.tsx` — counts per `issue.priority` (defaults to 0 for unset).\n- Row label: fixed-width marker column matching the Backlog pattern — `!!!` red (Urgent), `!!` warning/orange (High), `!` muted (Medium), em-dash placeholder for Low / No priority — followed by the priority name.\n- **Sort by priority order**, not by count: Urgent → High → Medium → Low → No priority. Priorities have inherent ordering, count sort would be misleading.\n- Only priorities with nonzero counts appear in the list.\n\n## Verification\n\n`make frontend` builds cleanly. Manually tested with issues across all five priority values."},"created_at":"2026-05-26T11:54:03.404229848Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
