{"id":"beats-e1ee26","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","sort_order":"a2"},"created_at":"2026-05-27T14:16:37.59740633Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-e1ee26","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-d270e55c-4f09-4b8f-8bb0-1f2aa1285975","text":"## Board DnD — walkthrough\n\nRewrote [web/src/components/Board/Board.tsx](web/src/components/Board/Board.tsx) on top of `@dnd-kit/core`, matching the pattern established in Backlog ([beats-d918bd](#)).\n\n### Interactions implemented\n\n- **Card → column body / column header** → status change, sorted to the end of the target column.\n- **Card → card** → position above/below the target card. Same column = pure reorder; different column = status change + insertion at the chosen position.\n- **Within-column reorder** → uses the existing fractional-key `generateKeyBetween` mechanism (same as Backlog).\n- **Same-status drag onto self** → no-op.\n\n### Visual feedback\n\n- **Column highlight** — `ring-2` accent ring + faint accent background on the targeted column when hovering empty space or the column header.\n- **Drop indicator** — 2px accent-coloured line at the top or bottom of the target card.\n- **Dragged source** — `opacity-40` on the original card (same as Backlog).\n- **Drag overlay** — `BoardCard` rendered with `shadow-lg` and `cursor-grabbing`, follows the pointer.\n\n### Sort behaviour\n\nCards within each column are sorted by manual `sort_order` via `sortGroup(..., 'manual')` from [web/src/utils/sort.ts](web/src/utils/sort.ts). This is hardcoded (no UI toggle yet) since DnD is the Board's primary interaction model. If a card has no `sort_order`, `getEffectiveKeys` generates virtual keys from creation date so it slots in deterministically.\n\n### Sensor\n\n`PointerSensor` with `activationConstraint: { distance: 3 }` — matches the tuning we landed on in Backlog. `KeyboardSensor` is also registered for basic keyboard drag (tab → space → arrows → space).\n\n### What's *not* in this PR\n\n- **No ALT-nest** — Board doesn't render sub-issue hierarchy; sub-issues appear as their own cards in their respective status columns. Cross-column drops do not touch `parent_id` (same lesson as [beats-93b04d](#)).\n- **No `Cmd`/`Ctrl` precise-slot modifier** — Board only has one drop mode per target: column body = end-of-column; card = above/below. No ambiguity to disambiguate.\n- **No batch-move** — sub-issue batch-move was a Backlog-specific behavior (because Backlog renders the tree). Board cards are independent units.\n- **No \"load all DONE during drag\"** — drops into the truncated DONE column still work; the new card slots in at the correct position based on `sort_order`. The truncated cards just become visible after refresh if they're now in the top N.\n\n### Code shape\n\nAbout 280 LOC total, of which ~150 LOC is DnD machinery. The remaining ~130 LOC is the column/card rendering that existed before. Component breakdown:\n\n- `Board` — owns DnD state, wraps everything in `\u003cDndContext\u003e`, renders columns.\n- `BoardColumn` — `useDroppable` for the column body; renders cards.\n- `DraggableBoardCard` — `useDraggable` + `useDroppable` on the same node; renders the card + drop indicator lines.\n- `BoardCard` — visual card used both as the regular column card and the drag overlay (`isOverlay` flag swaps shadow + cursor).\n- `BoardCardContent` — shared inner content (title, id, labels, estimate, pending dot).\n\n### Verification\n\n- `bun run build` → clean, +2.91 KB raw / +0.78 KB gzipped (now 341.88 KB gzipped total — Board logic is small).\n- `bunx eslint src/components/Board/Board.tsx` → 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- `make test` → Go tests pass.\n\n### Manual test plan\n\n- [ ] Drag a card from PLANNED to DOING column body → status changes, card appears at end of DOING.\n- [ ] Drag a card onto another card in a different column → status changes, card inserts above/below the target.\n- [ ] Drag within the same column to reorder → `sort_order` updates, no status change.\n- [ ] Drop a card onto the empty space below the last card in a column → goes to end of column.\n- [ ] Clicking a card still opens the detail view (3px activation distance disambiguates).\n- [ ] Drag a card from PLANNED with a `parent_id` (sub-issue) into DOING → parent retained (verify in detail view).\n- [ ] DONE column truncation: drag a card into DONE → still works regardless of truncated state.\n- [ ] Keyboard: tab to a card → space → arrow keys → space → card moves.\n\nReady for review."},"created_at":"2026-05-27T13:31:03.996468352Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-e1ee26","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-9017e5d9-7f9e-40f1-80c4-8ca786192d44","text":"## Fix — unreliable drop indicator at column edges\n\n**Symptom:** dragging just above the first card or just below the last card didn't show the drop-indicator line. It only appeared after wiggling the mouse.\n\n**Cause:** `closestCenter` was returning either the column or a card depending on tiny pixel positioning, because the column's droppable rect spans the whole scroll area (including the padding above the first card and below the last card). When `closestCenter` picked the column, my code routed to \"drop to end of column\" / column highlight instead of computing above/below relative to the nearest card.\n\n**Fix:** small custom collision detection at [Board.tsx:39-48](web/src/components/Board/Board.tsx#L39-L48):\n\n```typescript\nconst boardCollision: CollisionDetection = (args) =\u003e {\n  const all = closestCenter(args);\n  const cards = all.filter((c) =\u003e !String(c.id).startsWith('column-'));\n  return cards.length \u003e 0 ? cards : all;\n};\n```\n\nCards take priority over columns. The column wins only when **no** card is colliding — i.e., the column is empty. With a populated column:\n\n- Drag above the first card → first card is the closest collision → above indicator on first card.\n- Drag below the last card → last card is the closest collision → below indicator on last card.\n- Drag into a different column with cards → nearest card in that column becomes the target with above/below.\n- Drag into an empty column → only the column collides → column highlight + drop to end.\n\nBuild + lint clean. Ready for re-test."},"created_at":"2026-05-27T14:20:27.236033386Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-36beb6","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"relates_to","source_id":"beats-36beb6","target_id":"beats-d918bd"},{"kind":"relates_to","source_id":"beats-36beb6","target_id":"beats-e1ee26"}],"description":"## Symptom\n\nIn the Backlog view, dragging an issue just above the first row of a populated group or just below the last row required wiggling the mouse to make the drop indicator line appear. Same root cause as the Board fix on [beats-e1ee26](#).\n\n## Cause\n\n`closestCenter` collision detection picks between row droppables and the group-header droppable based on distance. At column edges the group header sometimes wins, and the existing `overRaw.startsWith(\"group-\")` branch routes to \"drop to end of group\" / column highlight instead of computing above/below relative to the nearest row.\n\n## Fix\n\nCustom collision detection at [Backlog.tsx](web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx) that prioritizes row collisions over group collisions:\n\n```typescript\nconst backlogCollision: CollisionDetection = (args) =\u003e {\n  const all = closestCenter(args);\n  const rows = all.filter((c) =\u003e !String(c.id).startsWith(\"group-\"));\n  return rows.length \u003e 0 ? rows : all;\n};\n```\n\nThe group wins only when no row is colliding (i.e. the group is empty). With a populated group:\n\n- Drag above the first row → first row is the closest collision → above indicator on first row.\n- Drag below the last row → last row is the closest collision → below indicator on last row.\n- Cross-status drop into an empty group → only the group header collides → column highlight + drop to end.\n\n## Trade-off\n\nDropping directly on a populated group's header strip used to mean \"cross-status move to end of group\". After this fix, that interaction resolves to \"above first row\" of that group. Functionally similar (cross-status move into the group), just at the top instead of the end. Users who want to land at the end can drop below the last row.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `bun run build` → clean, type-checks.\n- `bunx eslint src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx` → 0 errors, 0 warnings.","labels":["bug","WebApp","UX"],"status":"DOING","title":"Backlog DnD: drop indicator unreliable above first row / below last row of a group"},"created_at":"2026-05-27T14:24:58.153042328Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-e1ee26","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-82bcbe21-b143-4f68-89dd-a8576ad781c5","text":"## Follow-up — position miscomputed when grab point ≠ card center\n\nThe collision-priority fix made the right card win, but the above/below decision still misfired (visible in the screenshot: indicator showed above the last card instead of below it when the cursor was clearly below the last card).\n\n**Cause:** the above/below comparison used `active.rect.current.translated.center`, which is the source rect after applying drag delta. That center sits wherever the source's geometric middle is — which is **not** where the cursor is unless the user grabbed the exact middle of the card. Grab a card near the top → translated center lags the cursor by half the card's height.\n\n**Fix:** track the live pointer Y via a `pointermove` listener while a drag is in flight and use that for the above/below decision. Initialized in `handleDragStart` from the activator event so the first `onDragOver` has a valid value.\n\n```typescript\nconst pointerYRef = useRef\u003cnumber\u003e(0);\n\nuseEffect(() =\u003e {\n  if (!activeId) return;\n  const onMove = (e: PointerEvent) =\u003e { pointerYRef.current = e.clientY; };\n  window.addEventListener('pointermove', onMove);\n  return () =\u003e window.removeEventListener('pointermove', onMove);\n}, [activeId]);\n\n// in onDragOver:\nconst position = pointerYRef.current \u003c overCenterY ? 'above' : 'below';\n```\n\nSame fix landed on [beats-36beb6](#) for Backlog — see comment there.\n\nBuild + lint clean. Ready for re-test."},"created_at":"2026-05-27T14:38:21.126054536Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-36beb6","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-c9699aa3-8b35-4cfd-b645-f3a4d62334bf","text":"## Also fixed: pointer-vs-rect-center mismatch\n\nSame fix as on [beats-e1ee26](#): the above/below decision now uses the live pointer Y (tracked via a `pointermove` listener while dragging) instead of `active.rect.current.translated.center`. The translated rect's center depends on where on the row the user grabbed it — for tall items or off-center grabs, the comparison was biased.\n\n`pointerYRef` is added alongside the existing `modifiersRef` in the same drag-time `useEffect`, and initialized in `handleDndStart` from the activator event."},"created_at":"2026-05-27T14:38:23.736143152Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
