{"id":"beats-901ece","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Currently we have built-in default labels hard-coded with `beats install`. It would be great if we could make the default label set configurable in the `.beats/config.yaml` file (name + color). The config would take precedence over built-in.","labels":["feature"],"title":"Make default labels configurable"},"created_at":"2026-05-28T06:50:56.725192961Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-901ece","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"sort_order":"a3G"},"created_at":"2026-05-28T06:51:01.272999607Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-725c2f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Add React error boundary","description":"Wrap the main content area in an `ErrorBoundary` so render errors show a recovery UI instead of white-screening the app.\n\nCurrently any uncaught exception during React rendering crashes the entire app with no feedback. A class-based error boundary (React's only supported pattern) at the top level will catch these and render a fallback with a retry action.","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"beats-0ed889","assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@nicbet-wsl.local\u003e","labels":["improvement"]},"created_at":"2026-05-28T07:07:28.502424394Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-781691","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Structured API error handling in frontend client","description":"The API client (`api/client.ts`) throws generic `new Error('...')` on every failure and most consumers silently swallow with `.catch(() =\u003e {})`. Server-returned error details (status codes, validation messages) are discarded.\n\n- [ ] Create an `ApiError` class that carries `status`, `statusText`, and the server's response body\n- [ ] Update all `client.ts` functions to throw `ApiError`\n- [ ] Update key consumers to surface meaningful errors instead of silent swallowing","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"beats-0ed889","assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@nicbet-wsl.local\u003e","labels":["improvement"]},"created_at":"2026-05-28T07:07:31.486450269Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-8b30be","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Add test coverage for internal/server handlers","description":"`internal/server/handlers.go` (594 lines, 13 handlers) has zero test coverage. Every other package (`beats`, `config`, `inputs`, `mcpserver`) has tests.\n\nTable-driven tests using `httptest.NewServer` against each handler, covering happy paths and key error cases (404, bad JSON, etc.).","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"beats-0ed889","assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@nicbet-wsl.local\u003e","labels":["improvement"]},"created_at":"2026-05-28T07:07:34.294429232Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-47011a","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Split server handlers.go by concern","description":"`handlers.go` mixes HTTP handlers, response type definitions, serialization helpers (`issueToResponse`), and business logic (activity filtering, history assembly).\n\nSplit into:\n- `handlers.go` — HTTP handler methods only\n- `responses.go` — response types + serialization helpers\n- Move activity/history assembly logic into `beats` package where it's testable without HTTP","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"beats-0ed889","assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@nicbet-wsl.local\u003e","labels":["improvement"]},"created_at":"2026-05-28T07:07:36.3607614Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-725c2f","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-05-28T07:07:46.932261046Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-725c2f","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-d5189c0c-d75e-4cf1-8175-dccd4664d665","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded `ErrorBoundary` class component in `ui/ErrorBoundary.tsx`. Wraps `renderContent()` in `App.tsx` so any uncaught render error shows a styled fallback with the error message and a \"Try Again\" button that resets the boundary and re-fetches data, instead of white-screening the app.\n\nThe fallback UI matches the existing \"Server Offline\" illustration style for visual consistency."},"created_at":"2026-05-28T07:08:50.413940039Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-725c2f","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-05-28T07:08:50.7252014Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-781691","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-05-28T07:08:59.730171379Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-781691","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-921781ba-d9a1-488e-b2bf-b63c660fbfef","text":"## Summary\n\n- Created `ApiError` class in `api/client.ts` that carries `status`, `statusText`, and the server's response body text\n- Replaced all per-function `if (!res.ok) throw new Error(...)` with a shared `request\u003cT\u003e()` helper that throws `ApiError` on non-2xx responses\n- Updated key consumers:\n  - `IssueDetail.saveDraft` — shows server error message in a toast instead of silent console.error\n  - `PropertySidebar.handleDelete` — logs structured ApiError message\n  - `NewIssueModal.handleCreate` — logs structured ApiError message\n  - `App.fetchData` — includes status code in the error state shown on the \"Server Offline\" screen\n- Background pollers (metrics, activity, instances) still silently swallow since they retry on a timer"},"created_at":"2026-05-28T07:11:26.771907768Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
