{"id":"beats-f2c913","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-05-31T08:07:07.696201Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-f2c913","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-dc0ebb2a-f56c-49a5-8029-80108a1b0147","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded the current user's avatar and name to the bottom of the sidebar navigation.\n\n**Backend:**\n- Added `GET /api/user` endpoint in `handlers.go` returning `{name, email}` as separate fields\n- Added `getUserNameEmail()` helper in `responses.go` to parse the `\"Name \u003cemail\u003e\"` identity string\n- Registered route in `router.go`\n\n**Frontend:**\n- Added `fetchUser()` API client function with `User` type in `client.ts`\n- Updated `Layout.tsx` to fetch the current user on mount and render it at the bottom of the sidebar using the existing `Avatar` component (Gravatar with initials fallback) plus the user's name\n\n**Rationale:** Reused the existing `Avatar` component which already handles Gravatar loading with MD5 hashing and graceful fallback to initials — no new avatar logic needed."},"created_at":"2026-05-31T08:16:26.494372Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
