{"id":"beats-308a37","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-f25bce9e-a71b-46a9-9ead-ff255447bb48","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded a progress chart to the cycle detail view showing scope, started, and completed over time.\n\n### Backend\n- **`internal/server/router.go`** — added `GET /api/cycles/{id}/progress` route\n- **`internal/server/handlers.go`** — `handleCycleProgress()` replays all events chronologically, day-by-day across the cycle's date range, tracking which issues are in the cycle and their statuses. Returns `{ days: [{ date, scope, started, completed }, ...] }`\n- For current cycles, the date range is capped at today\n\n### Frontend\n- **`web/src/api/types.ts`** — added `CycleProgressDay` and `CycleProgressResponse` interfaces\n- **`web/src/api/client.ts`** — added `fetchCycleProgress(cycleId)` function\n- **`web/src/components/Cycles/Cycles.tsx`** — added `ProgressChart` component:\n  - Pure SVG line chart, no external chart library\n  - Dashed grey line for **scope** (total issues in cycle)\n  - Yellow filled area for **started** (DOING + BLOCKED)\n  - Green filled area for **completed** (DONE)\n  - Grid lines, date axis labels, and a legend\n  - Renders in the stats sidebar between the progress bar and the breakdown section\n  - Only shows when there are 2+ data points"},"created_at":"2026-06-01T12:48:31.724945276Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-308a37","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-01T12:48:36.63595984Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-a2ace7","type":"CREATE","payload":{"assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@nicbet-wsl.local\u003e","description":"## Problem\n\nThe Cycles timeline view had three visual bugs:\n\n1. **Two lines highlighted** — both the current and upcoming cycle's vertical lines were accent-colored, instead of only the current cycle's line.\n2. **Wrong dot highlighted** — the dot at the top of the current cycle's row (visually the end boundary) was accent-filled, while the dot at the bottom (visually the start boundary) was gray. Since time flows upward in the timeline, the bottom dot is the start and should be highlighted.\n3. **Layout inconsistency** — Cycles, Labels, and Dependencies views were not centered / width-constrained to match the Overview layout (`max-w-7xl mx-auto`).\n\n## Fix\n\n- `lineColor`: highlight only `rowIdx === currentIdx` (the current cycle's own row)\n- `dotProps`: changed from status-based to position-based — the dot *below* the current cycle's row (`prevInTime?.status === 'current'`) gets accent; the current cycle's own separator dot becomes hollow\n- Cycle icons: reduced from `w-5 h-5` to `w-4 h-4`\n- Centered content in Cycles, Labels, and Dependencies views with `max-w-7xl mx-auto`","labels":["bug","WebApp"],"parent_id":"beats-c7b7c6","status":"DOING","title":"Bug: Cycles timeline highlights wrong line and dot"},"created_at":"2026-06-01T15:25:53.913816008Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-a2ace7","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-66185573-10a7-4e03-9a9f-04e16856b8cc","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed the Cycles timeline highlighting and layout:\n\n- **`lineColor()`** — changed from highlighting both `upcomingIdx..currentIdx` rows to only `rowIdx === currentIdx`, so only the current cycle's row line is accent-colored.\n- **`dotProps()`** — switched from status-based to position-based logic. The separator dot *below* the current cycle's row (where `prevInTime?.status === 'current'`) gets accent fill (the visual start boundary). The current cycle's own separator dot (visual end boundary) becomes hollow instead.\n- **`CycleIcon`** — all variants reduced from `w-5 h-5` to `w-4 h-4` with `w-2 h-2` inner SVGs.\n- **View centering** — added `max-w-7xl mx-auto` to Cycles, Dependencies, and Labels views to match the Overview layout.\n\nFiles changed: `web/src/components/Cycles/Cycles.tsx`, `web/src/components/Labels/Labels.tsx`, `web/src/components/Dependencies/Dependencies.tsx`."},"created_at":"2026-06-01T15:26:00.380371349Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
