{"id":"beats-3c2135","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@nicbet-wsl.local\u003e"},"created_at":"2026-06-03T07:20:39.128126688Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.160 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-3c2135","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-b997f058-72a9-488c-8a9d-e2244491e7f5","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented read-time inference of DOING status from remote git branches. When `beats list` (CLI, MCP, or web API) runs inside a git repo, it scans `git branch -r` for remote branches where a path segment starts with an issue ID. Matching issues with BACKLOG or PLANNED status are synthetically upgraded to DOING — without mutating `issues.db`.\n\n### Files changed\n\n- **`internal/model/types.go`** — added `InferredStatus bool` field to `Issue` struct (projection-only, never persisted)\n- **`internal/beats/branches.go`** (new) — `applyBranchInference()` runs `git branch -r`, parses branch names, and upgrades matching issues. Helper functions `listRemoteBranches()` and `branchMatchesIssue()` handle the git interaction and pattern matching.\n- **`internal/beats/projection.go`** — wired `applyBranchInference()` into `ProjectIssuesWithConfig()` after automations and cycle rollover\n- **`internal/ui/styles.go`** — added `StatusIconForIssue()` which returns `◉` for inferred DOING vs `●` for explicit DOING\n- **`internal/ui/list.go`** — switched from `StatusIcon()` to `StatusIconForIssue()` in the list renderer\n- **`internal/mcpserver/tools.go`** — added `IsInferred` field to `issueSummary` and `showOut` structs, mapped in `toSummary()` and `show()` handler\n- **`internal/server/responses.go`** — added `IsInferred` field to `IssueResponse`, mapped in `issueToResponse()`\n\n### Tests added\n\n- **`internal/beats/branches_test.go`** — 9 unit tests for `branchMatchesIssue` (matching/non-matching patterns), integration tests for `applyBranchInference` in non-git and real-git-remote scenarios\n- **`internal/ui/styles_test.go`** — 5 test cases for `StatusIconForIssue` (inferred vs explicit, edge cases)\n\n### Design rationale\n\n- **Read-time overlay** avoids merge conflicts in `issues.db` and keeps the event log as source of truth\n- **Always-on** (no config toggle) — when not in a git repo, the feature is a no-op\n- **Only upgrades BACKLOG/PLANNED** — DONE, BLOCKED, and already-DOING issues are never modified\n- **Subtle `◉` icon** distinguishes inferred status at a glance without breaking the visual language\n- **`is_inferred` API field** lets the web frontend add its own visual treatment independently"},"created_at":"2026-06-03T07:23:35.100301238Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.160 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-d0da9f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Start Work command: set DOING + create branch off main","description":"## Summary\n\nAdd a `beats start \u003cissue-id\u003e` CLI command (and corresponding web UI button / API endpoint) that automates the \"pick up an issue\" workflow:\n\n1. Transitions the issue status to **DOING**\n2. Creates a new git branch off `main` named `\u003cissue-id\u003e/\u003cslugified-title\u003e` (e.g. `beats-3c2135/fix-login-flow`)\n3. Checks out the new branch\n\nThis enforces the branch naming convention that powers the synthetic DOING inference from `beats-3c2135`, and eliminates the manual two-step process of creating a branch + updating status.\n\n### CLI interface\n\n```\nbeats start \u003cissue-id\u003e\n```\n\n- Fails gracefully if the working tree is dirty (uncommitted changes)\n- Fails if the issue is already DONE or BLOCKED\n- If a matching branch already exists, checks it out instead of creating a new one\n\n### Web UI\n\n- \"Start Work\" button on the issue detail view\n- Calls a new API endpoint (e.g. `POST /api/issues/:id/start`)\n- Returns the branch name so the frontend can display it\n\n### Considerations\n\n- Branch base should default to `main` but respect the repo's default branch\n- Title slugification: lowercase, replace spaces/special chars with hyphens, truncate to keep branch name reasonable\n- Should work alongside the branch inference feature — once the branch is pushed, other collaborators see it as DOING automatically","status":"PLANNED","dependencies":[{"source_id":"beats-d0da9f","target_id":"beats-3c2135","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["feature","CLI","WebApp"]},"created_at":"2026-06-03T07:34:27.854335863Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.160 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-51af4e","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Show change indicators for issues with remote branches","description":"## Summary\n\nWhen an issue has a matching remote branch (detected via the branch inference from `beats-3c2135`), display change indicators showing how much work has happened on that branch:\n\n- **Commit count** — `git rev-list --count main..\u003cbranch\u003e`\n- **Files changed** — `git diff --stat main...\u003cbranch\u003e` parsed for file count\n- **Insertions/deletions** — net lines added/removed\n\n### CLI display\n\nCompact annotation in `beats list` and `beats show` output, e.g.:\n\n```\nbeats-3c2135  ◉ DOING   feature   Fix login flow   [3 commits, 7 files, +142 -38]\n```\n\n### API / MCP\n\nAdd fields to the issue response when a branch is detected:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"branch\": \"origin/beats-3c2135/fix-login\",\n  \"branch_stats\": {\n    \"commits\": 3,\n    \"files_changed\": 7,\n    \"insertions\": 142,\n    \"deletions\": 38\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Web UI\n\nDisplay as a compact badge or expandable section on the issue card/detail view.\n\n### Considerations\n\n- Stats are computed at read time (not cached) — should be fast for typical branch sizes\n- Needs to determine the correct base branch (main/master/default) for the diff\n- Only shown when a matching remote branch exists — graceful no-op otherwise\n- Builds on the branch detection infrastructure from `beats-3c2135`","status":"PLANNED","dependencies":[{"source_id":"beats-51af4e","target_id":"beats-3c2135","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["feature","CLI","WebApp"]},"created_at":"2026-06-03T07:34:36.663117569Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.160 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-5fc0f1","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"View git diffs for issue branches","description":"## Summary\n\nAdd the ability to view the git diff for an issue's associated branch, enabling lightweight code review directly from the issue tracker.\n\n### CLI\n\n```\nbeats diff \u003cissue-id\u003e\n```\n\n- Runs `git diff main...\u003cbranch\u003e` for the matching remote branch\n- Pipes through pager (respects `$PAGER` / `git config core.pager`)\n- Supports `--stat` flag for summary-only view\n\n### Web UI\n\n- Render a diff viewer on the issue detail page (syntax-highlighted, file-by-file)\n- Likely requires a dedicated frontend component or integration with an existing diff rendering library\n\n### Considerations\n\n- Most ambitious of the git integration features — especially the web UI diff rendering\n- CLI version is straightforward (shell out to `git diff`)\n- Web version needs careful thought around large diffs, binary files, and performance\n- Could start with CLI-only and add web rendering as a follow-up\n- Builds on branch detection (`beats-3c2135`) and change indicators","status":"BACKLOG","dependencies":[{"source_id":"beats-5fc0f1","target_id":"beats-3c2135","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["feature","CLI","WebApp"]},"created_at":"2026-06-03T07:34:43.214910955Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.160 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-d0da9f","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@nicbet-wsl.local\u003e"},"created_at":"2026-06-03T07:50:31.838894152Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.160 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-d0da9f","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-5604b9ac-6cfb-4065-b45e-f392f80675b5","text":"## Summary\n\nEnhanced the `beats start` command to create a git branch alongside setting status to DOING. Added the full stack: CLI, client method, API endpoint, MCP tool, and web UI button.\n\n### Files changed\n\n**Backend (Go)**:\n- **`internal/beats/slug.go`** (new) — `Slugify()` converts titles to branch-friendly slugs (lowercase, hyphens, truncated to ~50 chars)\n- **`internal/beats/git.go`** (new) — git helpers: `DefaultBranch()`, `BranchExists()`, `CreateAndCheckoutBranch()`, `CheckoutBranch()`\n- **`internal/beats/start.go`** (new) — `Client.StartWork(id)` method: validates status, transitions to DOING, creates/checks out branch if in a git repo\n- **`cmd/beats/update.go`** — rewired `startCmd` to call `client.StartWork()` instead of raw `UpdateIssue`\n- **`internal/server/handlers.go`** — added `handleStartWork` for `POST /api/issues/{id}/start`\n- **`internal/server/router.go`** — registered the new endpoint\n- **`internal/mcpserver/tools.go`** — added `beats_start` MCP tool with `startIn`/`startOut` types and `start()` handler\n\n**Frontend (React)**:\n- **`web/src/api/client.ts`** — added `startWork(issueId)` API function\n- **`web/src/components/IssueDetail/PropertySidebar.tsx`** — added \"Start Work\" button (play icon, accent color), visible only when status is BACKLOG or PLANNED, calls the start endpoint and refreshes\n\n**Tests**:\n- **`internal/beats/slug_test.go`** — 11 test cases (special chars, unicode, truncation, empty)\n- **`internal/beats/start_test.go`** — 5 tests: non-git repo, DONE/BLOCKED rejection, branch creation, existing branch checkout\n\n### Design rationale\n\n- Branch creation only happens in git repos — in non-git contexts, `start` silently updates status only (no error)\n- Default branch detection via `git symbolic-ref refs/remotes/origin/HEAD` with \"main\" fallback\n- If a matching branch already exists, checks it out instead of failing\n- DONE and BLOCKED issues are rejected; already-DOING issues skip the status update but still create/checkout the branch\n- Web UI button is contextual — only shown for actionable statuses (BACKLOG, PLANNED)"},"created_at":"2026-06-03T07:54:35.430377017Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.160 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-3c2135","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-e515dd2a-d7fd-489b-a5bd-0966c4fd4061","text":"## Final update\n\nWeb UI now visually distinguishes inferred DOING status. The `StatusIcon` component accepts an `isInferred` prop and renders a dashed-outline + semi-transparent half-fill variant for branch-inferred DOING, vs the solid half-fill for explicit DOING. Updated across all views: backlog, board, issue detail, property sidebar, sub-issues, command palette, cycles, pending changes, and dashboard.\n\n**Frontend files changed:**\n- `web/src/api/types.ts` — added `is_inferred?: boolean` to `Issue` type\n- `web/src/components/ui/StatusIcon.tsx` — added `isInferred` prop, renders distinct DOING icon variant\n- 9 component files updated to pass `isInferred={issue.is_inferred}` to StatusIcon"},"created_at":"2026-06-03T08:06:09.663702954Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.160 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-d0da9f","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-c29fbce3-d4c9-45b9-98bc-aee4bf7e8673","text":"## Final update\n\nAdded web UI inferred status indicator as part of this feature's scope. The `StatusIcon` component now shows a visually distinct icon for branch-inferred DOING status across all views. See `beats-3c2135` completion comment for details."},"created_at":"2026-06-03T08:06:11.157232812Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.160 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
