{"id":"beats-148cee","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-3a1eedce-5bdb-4e16-8dfc-cd8a8cb7266a","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented `beats review [issue-id]` — a unified code review view from the terminal.\n\n### New files\n\n- **`internal/beats/review.go`** — git helpers: `CurrentBranch()`, `ResolveReviewIssue()` (resolves by ID or infers from current branch), `IssueIDFromBranch()`, `ListBranchCommits()` (parses `git log --oneline`), `ListFilesChanged()` (parses `git diff --numstat` + `--name-status`), `RunDiffPaged()` (pipes diff through user's `GIT_PAGER`/`core.pager`/`PAGER`/`less`), `gitPager()` (pager resolution chain)\n- **`internal/ui/review.go`** — `RenderReview()` renders the summary view: issue title + meta, branch → base header, HEAD SHA + stats, commit list, markdown description (via glamour), and per-file stats with colored status indicators (A=green, D=red, M=muted)\n- **`cmd/beats/review.go`** — cobra command wiring. Accepts optional issue ID, gathers review data from git, renders summary, then pipes full diff through pager\n- **`internal/beats/review_test.go`** — 3 integration tests: `TestCurrentBranch` (branch name detection), `TestListBranchCommits` (commit parsing with real repos), `TestListFilesChanged` (file stats + status detection with real repos)\n\n### Design decisions\n\n- **Data types live in `ui` package** (`ReviewCommit`, `ReviewFile`, `ReviewData`) to avoid an import cycle — `beats` already imports `ui` in `list.go`, so `ui` cannot import `beats`. The CLI command bridges them by converting `beats.CommitEntry`/`beats.FileStat` to the ui types.\n- **Pager resolution** follows git's own precedence: `GIT_PAGER` → `core.pager` → `PAGER` → `less`. The diff is piped with `--color=always` so delta/diff-so-fancy work automatically.\n- **Branch inference** reuses the segment-matching logic from branch detection — if any segment of the current branch starts with an issue ID, it matches."},"created_at":"2026-06-09T08:11:44.238892245Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.169 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-148cee","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-09T08:11:44.423338325Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.169 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-148cee","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-aa4d3f3d-e1bd-4eec-9233-02c2653b089e","text":"## Follow-up: local branch support\n\n`beats review` now works with local branches that haven't been pushed. `ResolveReviewIssue` calls `fillLocalBranchStats` which checks the current branch first, then scans all local branches via `git branch --format=%(refname:short)`. Stats are computed with the same `computeBranchStats` used for remote branches.\n\n**New helpers:** `findLocalBranch(issueID)`, `branchNameMatchesIssue(branch, issueID)`, `fillLocalBranchStats(issue)`\n\n**Test:** `TestFindLocalBranch` — verifies matching from current branch, matching from a different branch (scan), and no-match case."},"created_at":"2026-06-09T08:30:09.173980377Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.169 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-148cee","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-75f4de80-a351-4fd6-836b-f0a7001a6ab1","text":"## Final update\n\nRemoved the automatic diff paging — replaced with a simple hint line showing the `git diff` command the user can run directly. This respects the user's own pager/delta setup without beats trying to manage the pipe.\n\nRemoved `RunDiffPaged()` and `gitPager()` from `internal/beats/review.go`."},"created_at":"2026-06-09T08:38:23.694317812Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.169 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
