{"id":"beats-bbef03","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-c617d388-30a2-4436-b1d3-5999e68845e8","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented `beats merge [issue-id]` — merges an issue's branch into the default branch, records a `MERGE` event, and transitions the issue to `DONE`.\n\n### New files\n\n- **`internal/model/types.go`** — added `EventTypeMerge` constant and `MergePayload` struct (branch, base_sha, merge_sha, strategy)\n- **`internal/beats/merge.go`** — `MergeIssue()` client method: pre-flight checks (clean tree), checkout default branch, run merge with chosen strategy, record `MERGE` event, optionally delete branch. Helpers: `isWorkingTreeClean()`, `resolveRef()`, `runGitMerge()`, `deleteBranch()`\n- **`cmd/beats/merge.go`** — cobra command with `--squash`, `--ff`, `--delete-branch`, `--keep-branch` flags. Shows compact summary before merge, prompts for branch deletion if no flag given.\n- **`internal/beats/merge_test.go`** — `TestMergeIssue_Squash` (full integration: create repo, branch, commits, merge, verify DONE status + MERGE event), `TestMergeIssue_DirtyTree` (verifies clean-tree guard)\n\n### Modified files\n\n- **`internal/beats/projection.go`** — added `MERGE` case to projection: sets status to `DONE` and records the event\n- **`internal/server/responses.go`** — `MERGE` events now appear in the activity feed\n\n### Merge strategies\n\n- `--squash` — squash into single commit with `\u003cissue-id\u003e: \u003ctitle\u003e` message\n- `--ff` — fast-forward only, fails if not possible\n- default — merge commit via `--no-ff`\n\n### Error handling\n\n- Dirty working tree → abort with message\n- Merge conflicts → abort merge, tell user to resolve manually\n- No branch found → helpful error\n- No commits ahead → clean exit"},"created_at":"2026-06-09T08:44:53.6177315Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.169 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
