{"id":"beats-0c592b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\nAdd an SSE endpoint so that connected clients receive live updates when issues change. In distributed mode this is essential — without it, every developer stares at stale data until they manually refresh.\n\n## Design\n\n### Server endpoint\n\n`GET /api/events` — SSE stream, requires bearer auth. The server maintains a set of connected clients. When any write operation completes (event appended to issues.db), the server broadcasts a notification to all connected SSE clients.\n\nEvent format:\n\n```\nevent: issue_updated\ndata: {\"issue_id\": \"beats-abc123\", \"type\": \"UPDATE\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-10T...\"}\n\nevent: issue_created\ndata: {\"issue_id\": \"beats-def456\", \"type\": \"CREATE\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-10T...\"}\n\nevent: issue_merged\ndata: {\"issue_id\": \"beats-abc123\", \"type\": \"MERGE\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-10T...\"}\n```\n\nKeep it lightweight — the event payload is a notification, not the full issue state. Clients fetch the updated issue via the normal REST API when they receive a notification.\n\n### Server implementation\n\n- Hub pattern: a central broadcaster with a channel per connected client\n- On event append: broadcast the event type + issue ID to all connected clients\n- Client disconnect: remove from hub, clean up channel\n- Heartbeat: send a `:keepalive` comment every 30s to detect dead connections\n\n### Proxy support\n\n`beats board` in remote proxy mode forwards the SSE stream from the remote to the browser. Standard HTTP reverse proxy handles this — SSE is just a long-lived HTTP response with `Content-Type: text/event-stream`.\n\n### Frontend\n\nThe web UI opens an `EventSource` connection to `/api/events`. On receiving a notification:\n\n- Refetch the affected issue (or the full issue list if simpler)\n- Update the UI reactively — board moves, status changes, new comments appear without manual refresh\n\nReplace the current polling pattern (if any) with SSE-driven invalidation.\n\n### Local mode\n\nIn local mode, SSE is not needed — there's only one user. The endpoint can exist but won't fire events (no concurrent writers). No changes to local mode behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `GET /api/events` SSE endpoint with bearer auth\n- [ ] Server broadcasts on every event append\n- [ ] Hub pattern with client registration/cleanup\n- [ ] Heartbeat keepalive every 30s\n- [ ] `beats board` proxy forwards SSE stream in remote mode\n- [ ] Frontend `EventSource` connection with automatic reconnect\n- [ ] UI refreshes on receiving update notifications\n- [ ] Graceful degradation: if SSE disconnects, fall back to polling","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","WebApp"],"parent_id":"beats-075586","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Real-time updates via Server-Sent Events"},"created_at":"2026-06-10T12:57:44.150968775Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.169 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
