{"id":"beats-c5c768","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\nIntroduce a transport layer in the `Client` struct so that every CLI command and MCP tool handler works transparently in both local and remote mode.\n\n## Design\n\nDefine a `Transport` interface:\n\n```go\ntype Transport interface {\n    ListIssues(opts FilterOptions) ([]*model.Issue, error)\n    GetIssue(id string) (*model.Issue, error)\n    UpdateIssue(id string, payload model.UpdatePayload, action string) ([]string, error)\n    AddIssue(payload model.CreatePayload) (*model.Issue, error)\n    AddComment(issueID, text string) error\n    // ... all operations the Client currently exposes\n}\n```\n\nTwo implementations:\n\n- `LocalTransport` — wraps the current `storage.ReadEvents()` + `ProjectIssues()` logic. This is what exists today, just extracted behind the interface.\n- `RemoteTransport` — HTTP client that calls `GET /api/issues`, `POST /api/draft`, etc. with the bearer token from config.\n\n`NewClient(cfg)` checks `cfg.RemoteURL` — if set (and token present), uses `RemoteTransport`. Otherwise `LocalTransport`.\n\n## Key decisions\n\n- The interface boundary is at the operation level (list, get, update), NOT at the storage level (read events, append event). Remote mode doesn't expose the event log — it talks REST.\n- `RemoteTransport` reuses the same REST endpoints the web UI already consumes. No new API surface.\n- Branch-related operations (review, merge, branch stats) remain local-only — they need the git working tree. These should gracefully degrade or error in remote mode.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `Transport` interface defined\n\n- [ ] `LocalTransport` extracted from current `Client` methods\n\n- [ ] `RemoteTransport` implementing the interface via HTTP\n\n- [ ] `NewClient` auto-selects transport based on config\n\n- [ ] All existing CLI commands work unchanged in local mode\n\n- [ ] CLI commands work against a running server in remote mode\n\n- [ ] MCP tool handlers work in both modes","status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-06-11T12:18:17.729321136Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.170 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-c5c768","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-efa183f6-4cf9-450f-b658-dcef15f55ceb","text":"## Summary\n\nIntroduced a `Transport` interface in `internal/beats/` so the Client can operate in both local and remote mode.\n\n### Phase 1: LocalTransport extraction (pure refactor)\n- **`transport.go`** — `Transport` interface with 9 methods (ListIssues, GetIssue, FindIssue, AddIssue, UpdateIssue, AddComment, DeleteIssue, CheckDuplicates, GetUser) + `ErrLocalOnly` sentinel\n- **`local_transport.go`** — `LocalTransport` struct extracted from the old Client; implements Transport using the existing event-sourcing logic (storage → projection → validation → append)\n- **`client.go`** — rewritten as a thin delegation wrapper with `syncLocal()` to propagate `Collapse`/`UserOverride`. Git-only methods (`StartWork`, `MergeIssue`, `FillLocalBranchStats`, etc.) stay on Client and guard with `c.local != nil`\n- **`list.go`** — `FilterIssues` promoted to package-level function (`currentUser` param) so both transports can use it\n- All method receivers changed from `*Client` to `*LocalTransport` in `add.go`, `update.go`, `comment.go`, `delete.go`, `duplicates.go`, `user.go`\n- `DeleteIssue` on Transport takes plain `bool cascade`; Client wrapper preserves variadic for backward compat\n- Zero caller changes — all existing CLI, MCP, and server handler code works unchanged\n\n### Phase 2: RemoteTransport + config\n- **`remote_transport.go`** — `RemoteTransport` implementing Transport via HTTP calls to existing REST API endpoints. Private `apiIssue` struct + `apiIssueToModel` conversion. Uses generics for `decodeJSON[T]`.\n- **`config.go`** — added `RemoteConfig{URL, Token}` to Config struct\n- **`NewClient`** — auto-selects transport: if `cfg.Remote.URL` is set, uses `RemoteTransport`; otherwise `LocalTransport`\n- **`remote_transport_test.go`** — 12 tests using `httptest.NewServer` covering all Transport methods, filtering, auth header, user caching, error handling\n\n### Rationale\n- Interface at operation level (not storage level) so RemoteTransport can map to existing REST endpoints without exposing the event log\n- `apiIssue` private struct avoids importing from `internal/server` (no circular deps)\n- Git operations remain local-only with `ErrLocalOnly` guard — they inherently need a working tree"},"created_at":"2026-06-11T12:10:36.08089668Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.170 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
