{"id":"beats-23dc97","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-670d673d-2d35-49aa-b913-071572777ba9","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented the SSH key auth system as a standalone `internal/auth/` package with full server integration.\n\n### New package: `internal/auth/` (6 files)\n- **`auth.go`** — `UserIdentity` type, `ParseIdentity()`, context helpers (`WithUser`, `UserFromContext`)\n- **`nonce.go`** — `NonceStore` with thread-safe in-memory map, 5-min TTL, single-use enforcement, passive cleanup\n- **`serverkey.go`** — `LoadOrGenerateServerKey()` — auto-generates ed25519 key in PEM (PKCS8) format with 0600 permissions\n- **`keys.go`** — `AuthorizedKeys` parser using `ssh.ParseAuthorizedKey()`, `Lookup()` via public key byte comparison\n- **`jwt.go`** — Hand-rolled JWS with EdDSA: `SignToken()` / `VerifyToken()` using `crypto/ed25519` + `base64.RawURLEncoding`, no third-party JWT library\n- **`middleware.go`** — `RequireAuth()` middleware: extracts Bearer token, verifies JWT, injects `UserIdentity` into request context\n\n### Server integration\n- **`server.go`** — added `NonceStore`, `AuthorizedKeys`, `SigningKey`, `VerifyKey` fields (nil when auth disabled)\n- **`router.go`** — `handle()` helper conditionally wraps all `/api/*` routes with auth middleware; auth endpoints (`POST /auth/challenge`, `POST /auth/verify`) and `/healthz` are public\n- **`handlers.go`** — `handleAuthChallenge` (nonce generation), `handleAuthVerify` (SSH signature verification → JWT issuance, 7-day expiry), `handleDraft` now sets `client.UserOverride` from auth context, `handleGetUser` respects auth identity\n\n### Dependencies\n- Added `golang.org/x/crypto/ssh` (upgraded `golang.org/x/crypto` to v0.53.0)\n\n### Tests: 34 new tests\n- **Auth unit tests (30)**: identity parsing, context round-trip, nonce generation/validation/single-use/expiry, server key generation/loading/bad-file, authorized_keys parsing/lookup/multiple-keys, JWT sign/verify/expiry/bad-sig/wrong-key/malformed, middleware valid/missing/invalid-scheme/expired/tampered\n- **Integration tests (4)**: full challenge→verify→authenticated API call flow, 401 without token, healthz always public, nonce replay prevention\n\n### Rationale\n- Standalone `internal/auth/` package for testability and reuse across `board` and upcoming `serve` commands\n- Hand-rolled JWT instead of third-party library — only ~50 lines, fixed algorithm (EdDSA), no negotiation needed\n- Auth is opt-in: nil auth fields = no middleware, backward-compatible with local `board` mode"},"created_at":"2026-06-11T12:37:23.405021235Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.170 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
