{"id":"beats-6c89d2","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-c72f9ea0-ecee-4452-a614-de6e8fca3e48","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded file-based locking for git-mutating operations to prevent concurrent working tree corruption.\n\n### Changes\n\n**`internal/beats/gitlock.go`** — new `WithGitLock(fn)` helper that acquires an exclusive flock on `.beats/git.lock` before running `fn`. Uses `github.com/gofrs/flock` for cross-platform support. 30-second timeout with 250ms retry interval. Lock is auto-released on process crash by the OS kernel.\n\n**`internal/beats/start.go`** — wrapped branch checkout/creation in `WithGitLock`\n\n**`internal/beats/merge.go`** — wrapped the entire merge operation (checkout base, merge, commit, branch delete) in `WithGitLock`\n\n**`internal/beats/gitlock_test.go`** — tests for serialization (5 goroutines contend, max concurrency stays at 1) and error propagation\n\n### What's NOT locked (by design)\n- Read-only git operations: diff computation, branch stats, review\n- Issue status transitions (handled by the event log mutex)\n- The lock only covers working tree mutations where concurrent access would corrupt state\n\n### Dependency added\n- `github.com/gofrs/flock` v0.13.0 — cross-platform file locking (Linux, macOS, Windows)"},"created_at":"2026-06-12T11:55:32.153390421Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.175 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
