{"id":"beats-d429a6","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\\n\\nAdd structured filtering to the Backlog view so users can narrow down issues by label, assignee, priority, and parent/epic — beyond the existing text search and status tabs.\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n- **Status tabs** — All Issues / Active / Backlog (coarse status grouping)\\n- **Text search** — free-text match on title, ID, and label name\\n- No way to say \\\"show me all `bug` issues assigned to Alice\\\" without scanning manually\\n\\n## Design\\n\\n### Filter bar\\n\\nA horizontal bar between the status tabs and the issue list. Hidden by default — toggled via a **funnel icon button** in the toolbar (next to sort). When active, shows filter chips.\\n\\n```\\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\\n│  All Issues   Active   Backlog          🔍  ⇅ Sort  ▽  │\\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\\n│  [Label ▾]  [Assignee ▾]  [Priority ▾]  [Epic ▾]  ✕    │\\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\\n│  ▸ PLANNED (3)                                          │\\n│    BEATS-123  Fix login flow          bug   alice       │\\n│    ...                                                  │\\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\\n```\\n\\n### Filter types\\n\\n| Filter | Control | Values | Source |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| **Label** | multi-select popover | all labels in current issue set | derived from `issues` |\\n| **Assignee** | multi-select popover | all assignees + \\\"Unassigned\\\" | derived from `issues` |\\n| **Priority** | multi-select popover | Urgent, High, Medium, Low, No priority | static list |\\n| **Epic** | single-select popover | issues with `epic` label | derived from `issues` |\\n\\nEach filter button shows as a chip. When a selection is made, the chip updates to show the count or value: `Label: bug, feature` or `Assignee (2)`. An **✕** button on each chip clears that filter. A global **✕** at the end clears all filters.\\n\\n### Filter popovers\\n\\nReuse the existing `Popover` component. Each popover contains:\\n- A small search input at the top (for long lists)\\n- Checkbox rows with the option name and issue count\\n- \\\"Select all\\\" / \\\"Clear\\\" links at the bottom\\n\\nFor labels, show the `LabelBadge` component inline. For assignees, show the `Avatar` component.\\n\\n### Filter logic\\n\\n- Filters combine with **AND** across dimensions: `label:bug AND assignee:alice`\\n- Within a dimension, selections combine with **OR**: `label:bug OR label:feature`\\n- Filters compose with the existing text search and status tabs\\n- Empty filter (nothing selected) = no constraint (show all)\\n\\n### Persistence\\n\\n- Filter state saved to `localStorage` keyed by tab: `beats-backlog-filters-{tab}`\\n- Restored on mount, cleared when user clicks global clear\\n- Filter bar visibility also persisted: `beats-backlog-filters-visible`\\n\\n### Keyboard shortcuts\\n\\n- `F` toggles the filter bar (when not in an input)\\n- `Escape` within a filter popover closes it\\n\\n### Count badge\\n\\nWhen filters are active and the filter bar is collapsed, the funnel icon shows a small dot/badge indicating active filters so the user knows results are narrowed.\\n\\n## Implementation\\n\\n### New components\\n\\n- `FilterBar.tsx` — the horizontal bar with filter chips\\n- `FilterPopover.tsx` — reusable multi-select popover with search, checkboxes, counts\\n\\n### Modified\\n\\n- `Backlog.tsx` — filter state management, wire FilterBar into layout, extend `filteredIssues` chain\\n- Toolbar section — add filter toggle button\\n\\n### Filter state shape\\n\\n```typescript\\ninterface BacklogFilters {\\n  labels: string[];      // selected labels (OR)\\n  assignees: string[];   // selected assignees (OR), \\\"__unassigned__\\\" for none\\n  priorities: number[];  // selected priority values (OR), 0 = no priority\\n  epicId: string | null; // selected parent epic ID\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Filtering extension\\n\\nThe existing `filteredIssues` chain gets additional predicates:\\n\\n```typescript\\nconst filteredIssues = issues.filter(i =\u003e\\n  visibleStatuses.includes(i.status) \u0026\u0026\\n  matchesSearch(i, query) \u0026\u0026\\n  matchesLabels(i, filters.labels) \u0026\u0026\\n  matchesAssignee(i, filters.assignees) \u0026\u0026\\n  matchesPriority(i, filters.priorities) \u0026\u0026\\n  matchesEpic(i, filters.epicId)\\n);\\n```\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Filter bar with Label, Assignee, Priority, Epic filters\\n- [ ] Multi-select popovers with search, checkboxes, and counts\\n- [ ] Filters combine with AND across dimensions, OR within\\n- [ ] Composes with existing text search and status tabs\\n- [ ] Filter state persists in localStorage per tab\\n- [ ] Toggle filter bar with toolbar button and `F` key\\n- [ ] Active-filter indicator when bar is collapsed\\n- [ ] Global and per-filter clear buttons","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","WebApp"]},"created_at":"2026-06-12T12:09:11.618320305Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.175 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-d429a6","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\nAdd structured filtering to the Backlog view so users can narrow down issues by label, assignee, priority, and parent/epic — beyond the existing text search and status tabs.\n\n## Current State\n\n- **Status tabs** — All Issues / Active / Backlog (coarse status grouping)\n- **Text search** — free-text match on title, ID, and label name\n- No way to say \"show me all `bug` issues assigned to Alice\" without scanning manually\n\n## Design\n\n### Filter bar\n\nA horizontal bar between the status tabs and the issue list. Hidden by default — toggled via a **funnel icon button** in the toolbar (next to sort). When active, shows filter chips.\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  All Issues   Active   Backlog          🔍  ⇅ Sort  ▽  │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  [Label ▾]  [Assignee ▾]  [Priority ▾]  [Epic ▾]  ✕    │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  ▸ PLANNED (3)                                          │\n│    BEATS-123  Fix login flow          bug   alice       │\n│    ...                                                  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Filter types\n\n| Filter | Control | Values | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Label** | multi-select popover | all labels in current issue set | derived from `issues` |\n| **Assignee** | multi-select popover | all assignees + \"Unassigned\" | derived from `issues` |\n| **Priority** | multi-select popover | Urgent, High, Medium, Low, No priority | static list |\n| **Epic** | single-select popover | issues with `epic` label | derived from `issues` |\n\nEach filter button shows as a chip. When a selection is made, the chip updates to show the count or value: `Label: bug, feature` or `Assignee (2)`. An **✕** button on each chip clears that filter. A global **✕** at the end clears all filters.\n\n### Filter popovers\n\nReuse the existing `Popover` component. Each popover contains:\n- A small search input at the top (for long lists)\n- Checkbox rows with the option name and issue count\n- \"Select all\" / \"Clear\" links at the bottom\n\nFor labels, show the `LabelBadge` component inline. For assignees, show the `Avatar` component.\n\n### Filter logic\n\n- Filters combine with **AND** across dimensions: `label:bug AND assignee:alice`\n- Within a dimension, selections combine with **OR**: `label:bug OR label:feature`\n- Filters compose with the existing text search and status tabs\n- Empty filter (nothing selected) = no constraint (show all)\n\n### Persistence\n\n- Filter state saved to `localStorage` keyed by tab: `beats-backlog-filters-{tab}`\n- Restored on mount, cleared when user clicks global clear\n- Filter bar visibility also persisted: `beats-backlog-filters-visible`\n\n### Keyboard shortcuts\n\n- `F` toggles the filter bar (when not in an input)\n- `Escape` within a filter popover closes it\n\n### Count badge\n\nWhen filters are active and the filter bar is collapsed, the funnel icon shows a small dot/badge indicating active filters so the user knows results are narrowed.\n\n## Implementation\n\n### New components\n\n- `FilterBar.tsx` — the horizontal bar with filter chips\n- `FilterPopover.tsx` — reusable multi-select popover with search, checkboxes, counts\n\n### Modified\n\n- `Backlog.tsx` — filter state management, wire FilterBar into layout, extend `filteredIssues` chain\n- Toolbar section — add filter toggle button\n\n### Filter state shape\n\n```typescript\ninterface BacklogFilters {\n  labels: string[];      // selected labels (OR)\n  assignees: string[];   // selected assignees (OR), \"__unassigned__\" for none\n  priorities: number[];  // selected priority values (OR), 0 = no priority\n  epicId: string | null; // selected parent epic ID\n}\n```\n\n### Filtering extension\n\nThe existing `filteredIssues` chain gets additional predicates:\n\n```typescript\nconst filteredIssues = issues.filter(i =\u003e\n  visibleStatuses.includes(i.status) \u0026\u0026\n  matchesSearch(i, query) \u0026\u0026\n  matchesLabels(i, filters.labels) \u0026\u0026\n  matchesAssignee(i, filters.assignees) \u0026\u0026\n  matchesPriority(i, filters.priorities) \u0026\u0026\n  matchesEpic(i, filters.epicId)\n);\n```\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Filter bar with Label, Assignee, Priority, Epic filters\n- [ ] Multi-select popovers with search, checkboxes, and counts\n- [ ] Filters combine with AND across dimensions, OR within\n- [ ] Composes with existing text search and status tabs\n- [ ] Filter state persists in localStorage per tab\n- [ ] Toggle filter bar with toolbar button and `F` key\n- [ ] Active-filter indicator when bar is collapsed\n- [ ] Global and per-filter clear buttons"},"created_at":"2026-06-12T12:43:05.667913992Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.175 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-d429a6","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\nAdd structured filtering to the Backlog view so users can narrow down issues by label, assignee, priority, estimate, and parent/epic — beyond the existing text search and status tabs.\n\n## Current State\n\n- **Status tabs** — All Issues / Active / Backlog (coarse status grouping)\n- **Text search** — free-text match on title, ID, and label name\n- No way to say \"show me all `bug` issues assigned to Alice\" without scanning manually\n\n## Design\n\n### Filter menu (nested popover)\n\nA single **funnel icon button** in the Backlog toolbar. Clicking it opens a command-menu-style popover listing filter dimensions. Each dimension row has a `▸` chevron that opens a nested sub-menu with selectable values.\n\n```\n  ┌──────────────────────────┐\n  │ Add Filter...          F │\n  │──────────────────────────│\n  │ ◉ Status             ▸  │──┐\n  │ 👤 Assignee           ▸  │  │  ┌────────────────────────┐\n  │ ‼ Priority            ▸  │  │  │ Filter...              │\n  │ △ Estimate            ▸  │  └──│ ◉ Backlog        1     │\n  │ ● Labels              ▸  │     │ ○ Planned        3     │\n  │ ◇ Epic                ▸  │     │ ◎ In Progress    2     │\n  │ 📅 Cycle               ▸  │     │ ✓ Done           8     │\n  └──────────────────────────┘     └────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Filter dimensions\n\n| Dimension | Sub-menu type | Values | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Status** | multi-select with counts | BACKLOG, PLANNED, DOING, BLOCKED, DONE | static |\n| **Assignee** | multi-select with counts | all assignees + \"Unassigned\" | derived from `issues` |\n| **Priority** | multi-select | Urgent, High, Medium, Low, No priority | static |\n| **Estimate** | multi-select | values from active estimation system | from config |\n| **Labels** | multi-select with badges | all labels in issue set | derived from `issues` |\n| **Epic** | single-select | issues with `epic` label | derived from `issues` |\n| **Cycle** | single-select | current + recent cycles | from config/API |\n\n### Sub-menu behavior\n\nEach sub-menu popover contains:\n- A **search input** at the top for long lists (auto-focused)\n- **Checkbox rows** — each showing the value name, a visual indicator (status icon, label badge, avatar), and an issue count\n- Clicking a row toggles its checkbox\n- Selecting any value immediately applies the filter (no confirm button)\n- The sub-menu stays open for multi-select; close with Escape or clicking outside\n\n### Active filter chips\n\nWhen filters are active, they appear as small chips below the tab bar (or inline in the toolbar):\n\n```\n  All Issues   Active   Backlog      [Label: bug ✕] [Assignee: alice ✕]  ▽ Sort  ⊞\n```\n\nEach chip shows the dimension and selected values (or count if \u003e2). The **✕** on each chip clears that filter. If many filters are active, chips wrap or collapse with a \"+N more\" indicator.\n\n### Filter logic\n\n- Filters combine with **AND** across dimensions: `label:bug AND assignee:alice`\n- Within a dimension, selections combine with **OR**: `label:bug OR label:feature`\n- Filters compose with the existing text search and status tabs\n- Empty filter (nothing selected in a dimension) = no constraint for that dimension\n- Status filter is independent of the tab filter — tabs set the broad view, the status filter narrows within it\n\n### Persistence\n\n- Filter state saved to `localStorage` keyed by tab: `beats-backlog-filters-{tab}`\n- Restored on mount\n- Filter menu visibility is ephemeral (popover closes on outside click)\n\n### Keyboard\n\n- `F` opens the filter menu (when not in an input)\n- Arrow keys navigate the filter menu and sub-menus\n- `Escape` closes the current level (sub-menu → main menu → closed)\n- Type to search within a sub-menu\n\n### Active filter indicator\n\nWhen filters are active and the menu is closed, the funnel icon shows a small colored dot (like the reference design) so users know results are narrowed.\n\n## Implementation\n\n### New components\n\n- `FilterMenu.tsx` — the top-level popover with dimension rows\n- `FilterSubMenu.tsx` — reusable nested popover with search, checkboxes, counts\n- `FilterChips.tsx` — the active filter chip row\n\n### Modified\n\n- `Backlog.tsx` — filter state management, wire components into layout, extend `filteredIssues` chain\n- Toolbar section — add filter toggle button with active indicator\n\n### Filter state shape\n\n```typescript\ninterface BacklogFilters {\n  statuses: string[];    // selected statuses (OR)\n  labels: string[];      // selected labels (OR)\n  assignees: string[];   // selected assignees (OR), \"__unassigned__\" for none\n  priorities: number[];  // selected priority values (OR), 0 = no priority\n  estimates: number[];   // selected estimate values (OR)\n  epicId: string | null; // selected parent epic ID\n  cycleId: string | null; // selected cycle ID\n}\n\nconst EMPTY_FILTERS: BacklogFilters = {\n  statuses: [], labels: [], assignees: [],\n  priorities: [], estimates: [],\n  epicId: null, cycleId: null,\n};\n```\n\n### Filtering extension\n\nThe existing `filteredIssues` chain gets additional predicates:\n\n```typescript\nconst filteredIssues = issues.filter(i =\u003e\n  visibleStatuses.includes(i.status) \u0026\u0026\n  matchesSearch(i, query) \u0026\u0026\n  matchesStatuses(i, filters.statuses) \u0026\u0026\n  matchesLabels(i, filters.labels) \u0026\u0026\n  matchesAssignee(i, filters.assignees) \u0026\u0026\n  matchesPriority(i, filters.priorities) \u0026\u0026\n  matchesEstimate(i, filters.estimates) \u0026\u0026\n  matchesEpic(i, filters.epicId) \u0026\u0026\n  matchesCycle(i, filters.cycleId)\n);\n```\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Filter menu opens from funnel icon in toolbar\n- [ ] Nested sub-menus for each dimension with search, checkboxes, and counts\n- [ ] Active filter chips displayed below tabs showing current selections\n- [ ] Filters combine with AND across dimensions, OR within\n- [ ] Composes with existing text search and status tabs\n- [ ] Filter state persists in localStorage per tab\n- [ ] `F` keyboard shortcut to open filter menu\n- [ ] Active-filter dot indicator on funnel icon when filters are set\n- [ ] Per-filter and global clear via chip ✕ buttons"},"created_at":"2026-06-12T13:08:59.117144887Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.175 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-d429a6","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\nAdd structured filtering to the Backlog view so users can narrow down issues by label, assignee, priority, estimate, and parent/epic — beyond the existing text search and status tabs.\n\n## Current State\n\n- **Status tabs** — All Issues / Active / Backlog (coarse status grouping)\n- **Text search** — free-text match on title, ID, and label name\n- No way to say \"show me all `bug` issues assigned to Alice\" without scanning manually\n\n## Design\n\n### Filter menu (nested popover)\n\nA single **funnel icon button** in the Backlog toolbar (next to Sort). Clicking it opens a command-menu-style popover listing filter dimensions. Each dimension row has a `▸` chevron that opens a nested sub-menu with selectable values.\n\n```\n  ┌──────────────────────────┐\n  │ Add Filter...          F │\n  │──────────────────────────│\n  │ ◉ Status             ▸  │──┐\n  │ 👤 Assignee           ▸  │  │  ┌────────────────────────┐\n  │ ‼ Priority            ▸  │  │  │ Filter...              │\n  │ △ Estimate            ▸  │  └──│ ◉ Backlog        1     │\n  │ ● Labels              ▸  │     │ ○ Planned        3     │\n  │ ◇ Epic                ▸  │     │ ◎ In Progress    2     │\n  │ 📅 Cycle               ▸  │     │ ✓ Done           8     │\n  └──────────────────────────┘     └────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Filter dimensions\n\n| Dimension | Sub-menu type | Values | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Status** | multi-select with counts | BACKLOG, PLANNED, DOING, BLOCKED, DONE | static |\n| **Assignee** | multi-select with counts | all assignees + \"Unassigned\" | derived from `issues` |\n| **Priority** | multi-select | Urgent, High, Medium, Low, No priority | static |\n| **Estimate** | multi-select | values from active estimation system | from config |\n| **Labels** | multi-select with badges | all labels in issue set | derived from `issues` |\n| **Epic** | single-select | issues with `epic` label | derived from `issues` |\n| **Cycle** | single-select | current + recent cycles | from config/API |\n\n### Sub-menu behavior\n\nEach sub-menu popover contains:\n- A **search input** at the top for long lists (auto-focused)\n- **Checkbox rows** — each showing the value name, a visual indicator (status icon, label badge, avatar), and an issue count\n- Clicking a row toggles its checkbox\n- Selecting any value immediately applies the filter (no confirm button)\n- The sub-menu stays open for multi-select; close with Escape or clicking outside\n\n### Active filter chips in the status bar\n\nWhen filters are active, they appear as small chips in the **bottom status bar** (left side), next to the existing connection indicator (right side). This avoids adding a second row below the tabs and keeps filters always visible.\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                          main content                              │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ [Status: Planned, Doing ✕] [Label: bug ✕]  ✕     ● Beats v0.3.0  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n**Chip design:**\n- Each chip shows dimension name + selected values (or count if \u003e2 values): `Label: bug, feature` or `Assignee (3)`\n- **✕** on each chip clears that dimension's filter\n- A standalone **✕** after all chips clears all filters\n- Chips are compact (small text, low-profile styling matching the status bar's muted aesthetic)\n- When no filters are active, the left side of the status bar is empty (no visual noise)\n\nThe status bar is part of `Layout.tsx` so filter chips are visible on every view, but only populated when the Backlog view has active filters. Other views ignore them.\n\n### Filter logic\n\n- Filters combine with **AND** across dimensions: `label:bug AND assignee:alice`\n- Within a dimension, selections combine with **OR**: `label:bug OR label:feature`\n- Filters compose with the existing text search and status tabs\n- Empty filter (nothing selected in a dimension) = no constraint for that dimension\n- Status filter is independent of the tab filter — tabs set the broad view, the status filter narrows within it\n\n### Persistence\n\n- Filter state saved to `localStorage` keyed by tab: `beats-backlog-filters-{tab}`\n- Restored on mount\n\n### Keyboard\n\n- `F` opens the filter menu (when not in an input)\n- Arrow keys navigate the filter menu and sub-menus\n- `Escape` closes the current level (sub-menu → main menu → closed)\n- Type to search within a sub-menu\n\n### Active filter indicator\n\nWhen filters are active, the funnel icon in the toolbar shows a small colored dot so users know results are narrowed even without looking at the status bar.\n\n## Implementation\n\n### New components\n\n- `FilterMenu.tsx` — the top-level popover with dimension rows\n- `FilterSubMenu.tsx` — reusable nested popover with search, checkboxes, counts\n- `FilterChips.tsx` — the chip row rendered inside the Layout status bar\n\n### Modified\n\n- `Backlog.tsx` — filter state management, wire FilterMenu, extend `filteredIssues` chain\n- `Layout.tsx` — accept optional `statusBarLeft` ReactNode prop, render filter chips in the status bar\n- `App.tsx` — pass filter chips from Backlog state down to Layout\n- Toolbar section — add filter toggle button with active indicator\n\n### Filter state shape\n\n```typescript\ninterface BacklogFilters {\n  statuses: string[];    // selected statuses (OR)\n  labels: string[];      // selected labels (OR)\n  assignees: string[];   // selected assignees (OR), \"__unassigned__\" for none\n  priorities: number[];  // selected priority values (OR), 0 = no priority\n  estimates: number[];   // selected estimate values (OR)\n  epicId: string | null; // selected parent epic ID\n  cycleId: string | null; // selected cycle ID\n}\n\nconst EMPTY_FILTERS: BacklogFilters = {\n  statuses: [], labels: [], assignees: [],\n  priorities: [], estimates: [],\n  epicId: null, cycleId: null,\n};\n```\n\n### Filtering extension\n\nThe existing `filteredIssues` chain gets additional predicates:\n\n```typescript\nconst filteredIssues = issues.filter(i =\u003e\n  visibleStatuses.includes(i.status) \u0026\u0026\n  matchesSearch(i, query) \u0026\u0026\n  matchesStatuses(i, filters.statuses) \u0026\u0026\n  matchesLabels(i, filters.labels) \u0026\u0026\n  matchesAssignee(i, filters.assignees) \u0026\u0026\n  matchesPriority(i, filters.priorities) \u0026\u0026\n  matchesEstimate(i, filters.estimates) \u0026\u0026\n  matchesEpic(i, filters.epicId) \u0026\u0026\n  matchesCycle(i, filters.cycleId)\n);\n```\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Filter menu opens from funnel icon in Backlog toolbar\n- [ ] Nested sub-menus for each dimension with search, checkboxes, and counts\n- [ ] Active filter chips rendered in the bottom status bar (left side)\n- [ ] Filters combine with AND across dimensions, OR within\n- [ ] Composes with existing text search and status tabs\n- [ ] Filter state persists in localStorage per tab\n- [ ] `F` keyboard shortcut to open filter menu\n- [ ] Active-filter dot indicator on funnel icon when filters are set\n- [ ] Per-filter ✕ and global ✕ clear buttons on chips"},"created_at":"2026-06-13T06:15:07.270779483Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.175 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
