{"id":"beats-7d71cf","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-b306e1f6-ce7e-405d-9f66-fae3273ba3b1","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed new issues appearing in the middle of the backlog instead of at the end.\n\n### Root cause\n\nTwo interacting bugs:\n\n1. **`internal/beats/projection.go`** `backfillSortOrder` — assigns ephemeral sort keys to issues without a `sort_order` on every projection. Since Go map iteration is non-deterministic and the sort was unstable (issues with identical `CreatedAt` could swap), backfilled keys varied between projections. The frontend would compute an append key based on one projection's backfilled keys, but the next projection would produce different keys, placing the new issue in the middle.\n\n2. **`web/src/utils/sort.ts`** `computeAppendKey` — only considered issues in the same status group when finding the max key. This missed issues in other groups whose sort keys were higher, leading to new keys that weren't globally maximal.\n\n### Fixes\n\n- `backfillSortOrder`: added ID-based tiebreaker to the sort for deterministic ordering when timestamps match\n- `computeAppendKey`: changed to find the global max `sort_order` across all issues, guaranteeing new issues always sort last"},"created_at":"2026-06-13T06:40:35.411260582Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.175 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-7d71cf","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-13T06:40:46.322597748Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.175 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
