{"id":"beats-97ec68","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-d077ca73-abdb-494d-8b4a-767b693a8165","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed drag-and-drop sorting to allow dropping above the first item in a backlog group.\n\n### Root cause\n\nTwo interacting issues:\n\n1. **`onDragOver` only fires when the over target changes**, not continuously as the pointer moves. The above/below position was calculated in `onDragOver`, so it was only set once when entering an item's zone — if you entered from below, \"below\" was set and never updated to \"above\" even as the pointer moved up.\n\n2. **Group header collision** — when dragging above the first item, the pointer enters the group header's droppable zone. `backlogCollision` filtered out group headers in favor of issue rows, but the position was already locked to \"below\" from the initial entry.\n\n### Fix\n\n**`web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx`**:\n- Moved the above/below position calculation from `onDragOver` to a new `onDragMove` handler (fires continuously during drag)\n- `onDragMove` uses `getBoundingClientRect()` on the actual DOM element (via `data-row` attribute) for accurate position comparison\n- `onDragMove` handles both group headers (shows \"above first issue\" for same-group drags) and issue rows\n- Cross-group drags without meta/ctrl key suppress the indicator (only group highlight shows)\n- `onDragOver` now only handles target detection, group/nest highlighting, and clearing state"},"created_at":"2026-06-13T08:17:22.863071888Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.175 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-97ec68","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-13T08:17:27.525357931Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.175 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
