{"id":"beats-520aeb","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-d900078d-b057-4cf4-ae04-eb0130211ab4","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented velocity charts and flow statistics for the Overview dashboard.\n\n### Backend — `internal/server/metrics.go`\n\n- Added 14-day daily velocity buckets (`daily_buckets`) to the velocity response\n- Added velocity delta (last 7d vs prior 7d points)\n- Added flow metrics: cycle time, lead time (min/median/p75/p90/max in hours), and staleness distribution\n- Fixed negative cycle times by guarding `doneAt \u003e doingAt`\n\n### Frontend — Charts (`web/src/components/Dashboard/charts.tsx`)\n\n- `DailyVelocityChart` — Recharts step area chart, full-width, 14 daily ticks\n- `CumulativeChart` — Recharts cumulative area chart for created vs completed\n- `TrendChart` — Recharts bar chart (kept for future use)\n- `DistributionBar` — kept for future use\n\n### Frontend — Dashboard (`web/src/components/Dashboard/`)\n\nPulse section restructured:\n- **Top row (50/50)**: Created vs Completed cumulative chart | Daily Velocity step chart\n- **Bottom row (4 cards)**: Velocity (big number + sparkline, vertically centered) | Cycle Time (bordered table: Min/Median/P90/Max) | Lead Time (same table format) | Staleness (bar distribution)\n- All legends pinned to card bottom for consistent visual hierarchy\n- Backend reports hours, frontend auto-formats to best unit (m/h/d/w/mo) via `formatDuration`\n\nOther changes:\n- Moved Composition section between Pulse and Activity\n- Added \"By Status\" distribution card showing all 5 statuses\n- Labels use color dot + name instead of badge style\n- Status card hides progress bars\n- Bars scaled relative to total, not max\n- Default filter changed to \"All\"\n- Auto-hide scrollbars on composition cards\n- Removed Trends section and status count cards from view (code kept)\n- Added `recharts` dependency"},"created_at":"2026-06-13T10:05:21.610940555Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.175 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-520aeb","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-13T10:05:28.877759092Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.175 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-38a287","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Overview: Composition cards should have uniform height","description":"In the **Overview** view, the \"Composition\" cards have inconsistent heights depending on how many items they contain.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\n- All Composition cards should have a **fixed height** sized to fit **5 items**.\n- When a card has **more than 5 items**, its content should scroll (current behavior — keep as-is).\n- When a card has **fewer than 5 items**, the card should maintain the same fixed height with empty space below the items.\n\n## Why\n\nUniform card heights create a cleaner, more visually consistent layout and prevent cards from jumping around or causing uneven rows.","status":"PLANNED","labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-06-14T07:10:55.917636617Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.176 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-38a287","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-06-14T07:15:01.183146888Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.176 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-38a287","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-bb1e5e14-73d7-4081-be7b-ba292e208bf9","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed Composition cards in the Overview to have uniform height regardless of item count.\n\n### Change — `web/src/components/Dashboard/DistributionSection.tsx`\n\n- Content list: changed `max-h-40` → `h-40` so the list area is always 160px tall. Cards with fewer than 5 items now show empty space; cards with more still scroll as before.\n- Empty state: changed `flex-1` → `h-40` so zero-item cards match the same height.\n- Outer card: removed `min-h-40` since both branches now enforce height directly."},"created_at":"2026-06-14T07:33:47.567250071Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.176 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-38a287","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-14T07:33:48.028114748Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.176 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-213d27","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"beats-213d27","target_id":"beats-7cd82d"}],"description":"## Summary\n\nA dedicated Inbox view in the web UI that surfaces events relevant to the current user — assignments, comments on their issues, status changes, and merges. The browser counterpart to the CLI `beats inbox` command (`beats-7cd82d`).\n\n## Design\n\n### Navigation\n\n- New **Inbox** entry in the sidebar, slotted above Dashboard.\n- Unread count badge on the nav item (e.g. \"Inbox (3)\").\n- Badge disappears when all items are read.\n\n### Inbox View\n\nA reverse-chronological feed of events relevant to the authenticated user. Each entry shows:\n\n- Relative timestamp (\"2m ago\", \"1h ago\")\n- Actor avatar / initials\n- Event description (e.g. \"alice assigned beats-abc123 to you\")\n- Click-through to the referenced issue\n\n### What's \"relevant to you\"\n\nSame filtering rules as the CLI inbox:\n\n- Events on issues where the user is the **assignee**\n- Events on issues where the user is the **creator**\n- Events on issues where the user is a **commenter** (participated in conversation)\n- All **merge** events (team-wide visibility)\n\n### Read Tracking\n\n- Individual items can be marked as read (click or swipe).\n- **\"Mark all as read\"** button at the top.\n- Read state persisted via API — survives page refresh and cross-tab.\n- Unread items visually distinct (bold / highlight vs muted).\n\n### API\n\nConsumes the REST endpoints established by the CLI inbox feature:\n\n- `GET /api/inbox` — returns filtered events for the authenticated user, with read/unread state\n- `POST /api/inbox/read` — mark items as read (accepts list of event IDs or `\"all\"`)\n\n### Real-time\n\nLeverage the existing SSE infrastructure (`useSSE` hook) to push new inbox items to the browser in real-time — no polling needed. New events bump the unread badge count.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Inbox nav item in sidebar with unread count badge\n- [ ] Inbox view displays events filtered to the current user\n- [ ] Events are clickable — navigate to the referenced issue\n- [ ] Individual mark-as-read and bulk \"mark all read\"\n- [ ] Read state persists across page refreshes\n- [ ] Real-time updates via SSE (new events appear without reload)\n- [ ] Works in local mode (scan event log, filter by git identity)\n- [ ] Works in distributed mode (server-side filtering via `/api/inbox`)","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","WebUI"],"parent_id":"beats-075586","status":"BACKLOG","title":"WebUI Inbox: personal notification feed in the browser"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T05:42:11.551567444Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-7cd82d","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-cf9fb224-a2c3-479d-8d56-9dc58e1b6fa2","text":"## Design decision: inbox read timestamp location\n\nThe read timestamp is **per-user state** and must not live in `.beats/` (which is shared project state). Even in local mode, multiple developers (and agents) may pull the same event log — each needs their own read cursor.\n\n### Location\n\n`~/.config/beats/inbox.yaml`, alongside the existing `credentials.yaml`. The `credentialsPath()` helper in `internal/config/remote.go` already resolves the user config dir via `BEATS_CONFIG_DIR` env var or `~/.config/beats/` — the inbox file should use the same resolution logic.\n\n### Structure\n\n```yaml\nprojects:\n  # Local mode — keyed by absolute path to .beats dir\n  \"/home/alice/myproject/.beats\":\n    last_read: \"2026-06-15T10:30:00Z\"\n  # Distributed mode — keyed by server host\n  \"beats.internal\":\n    last_read: \"2026-06-15T10:30:00Z\"\n```\n\n### Invariant\n\nRead state is always per-user, never shared — regardless of local vs distributed mode."},"created_at":"2026-06-15T05:46:32.179866324Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-213d27","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-eccebda7-5ba5-4611-8ae9-af3f5873a366","text":"## Design decision: inbox read state storage\n\nPer discussion on `beats-7cd82d` — inbox read state is **per-user** and must not live in `.beats/`.\n\n### Location\n\n`~/.config/beats/inbox.yaml`, alongside the existing `credentials.yaml`. Reuses the same `BEATS_CONFIG_DIR` override / `~/.config/beats/` default from `credentialsPath()` in `internal/config/remote.go`.\n\n### Structure\n\n```yaml\nprojects:\n  # Local mode — keyed by absolute path to .beats dir\n  \"/home/alice/myproject/.beats\":\n    last_read: \"2026-06-15T10:30:00Z\"\n  # Distributed mode — keyed by server host\n  \"beats.internal\":\n    last_read: \"2026-06-15T10:30:00Z\"\n```\n\n### WebUI implications\n\n- **Local mode**: `beats board` serves the WebUI locally — the server process has access to `~/.config/beats/inbox.yaml` directly, so the `GET /api/inbox` handler can read/write the timestamp.\n- **Distributed mode**: the remote server stores read state per-user (keyed by JWT identity). The local proxy in `beats board` forwards the auth header, so the server knows which user's state to query.\n\nThe WebUI never reads `inbox.yaml` directly — it always goes through the API, which abstracts the storage location."},"created_at":"2026-06-15T05:46:38.378891427Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-7cd82d","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\n`beats inbox` shows events relevant to you since your last check — assignments, comments on your issues, status changes, merges. For developers working in the terminal who don't have the board open.\n\n## Design\n\n### CLI command\n\n```\n$ beats inbox\n  2m ago   alice assigned beats-abc123 to you\n  5m ago   bob commented on beats-def456 \"Looks good, one nit...\"\n  1h ago   alice merged beats-ghi789 via squash\n  3h ago   carol changed beats-abc123 status to BLOCKED\n\n3 new since last check. Run `beats inbox --clear` to mark as read.\n```\n\n### What's \"relevant to you\"\n\nEvents on issues where you are:\n- The assignee\n- The creator\n- A commenter (you've participated in the conversation)\n\nPlus all MERGE events (team-wide visibility).\n\n### Read tracking\n\nStore a per-user timestamp in `~/.config/beats/inbox.yaml` (alongside `credentials.yaml`), respecting the `BEATS_CONFIG_DIR` override. Keyed by project:\n\n```yaml\nprojects:\n  # Local mode — keyed by absolute path to .beats dir\n  \"/home/alice/myproject/.beats\":\n    last_read: \"2026-06-15T10:30:00Z\"\n  # Distributed mode — keyed by server host\n  \"beats.internal\":\n    last_read: \"2026-06-15T10:30:00Z\"\n```\n\n`beats inbox` shows events after that timestamp. `beats inbox --clear` updates the timestamp to now.\n\n**Invariant:** read state is always per-user, never in `.beats/` — even in local mode, multiple developers and agents may pull the same event log and each needs their own read cursor.\n\n### Distributed mode\n\nIn distributed mode, the server has all events. `beats inbox` calls `GET /api/inbox` which filters events server-side based on the authenticated user's identity.\n\n### Local mode\n\nIn local mode, scan the event log and filter by the git user identity. Less useful (you're the only user) but still handy for tracking what your agents did while you were away.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `beats inbox` shows recent events relevant to the current user\n- [ ] Events filtered by assignee, creator, commenter, plus merges\n- [ ] Per-user timestamp-based read tracking in `~/.config/beats/inbox.yaml`\n- [ ] `beats inbox --clear` marks all as read\n- [ ] Works in local mode (scan event log)\n- [ ] Works in distributed mode (server-side filtering)\n- [ ] Compact, readable terminal output"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T05:46:59.024753108Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-0a9e5b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\nReplace `~/.config/beats/credentials.yaml` with `~/.config/beats/user.yaml` as the single file for all per-user state. This consolidates credentials and future per-user concerns (inbox read tracking, preferences) into one file.\n\nNo migration path needed — distributed mode is not deployed yet.\n\n## Current state\n\n`internal/config/remote.go` reads/writes `~/.config/beats/credentials.yaml` with this structure:\n\n```yaml\nservers:\n  beats.internal:\n    url: https://beats.internal\n    token: eyJhbG...\n```\n\n## Target state\n\n`~/.config/beats/user.yaml` with the same structure, extended to hold per-server inbox state:\n\n```yaml\nservers:\n  beats.internal:\n    url: https://beats.internal\n    token: eyJhbG...\n    last_read: \"2026-06-15T10:30:00Z\"\n```\n\n## Implementation\n\n- [ ] Rename `credentialsPath()` → `userConfigPath()` in `internal/config/remote.go`, returning `user.yaml`\n- [ ] Update `Credentials` struct name and fields to reflect broader purpose (e.g. `UserConfig`)\n- [ ] Update `LoadCredentials` / `SaveCredentials` and callers\n- [ ] Update `cmd/beats/login.go` references\n- [ ] Keep `0600` file permissions (file still contains tokens)\n- [ ] Update tests in `internal/config/remote_test.go`\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `beats login` writes tokens to `~/.config/beats/user.yaml`\n- [ ] `BEATS_CONFIG_DIR` override still respected\n- [ ] File permissions remain `0600`\n- [ ] No references to `credentials.yaml` remain in the codebase","estimate":2,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"beats-075586","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Rename credentials.yaml to user.yaml as unified per-user config"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T05:49:28.263068905Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-7cd82d","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"source_id":"beats-7cd82d","target_id":"beats-834350","kind":"depends_on"},{"source_id":"beats-7cd82d","target_id":"beats-0a9e5b","kind":"depends_on"}]},"created_at":"2026-06-15T05:49:32.018289335Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
