{"id":"beats-b1a394","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"When updating the status on a parent issue with sub-issues we get atomic status updates for each child issues one by one instead of one bulk update (when auto transitions are configured).","labels":["bug"],"sort_order":"b56","title":"Bulk updates for status changes on parent and sub-issues"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T07:35:11.938539716Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-b1a394","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T07:35:12.274250616Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-b1a394","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T07:45:17.435342988Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-b1a394","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-8f506428-37a1-4d31-95dd-7c818be96883","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed parent+children status changes rendering one-by-one instead of as a single block.\n\n**Root cause:** The frontend's drag handler in `Backlog.tsx` was sending individual `addDraft` calls for each child in the batch (`await` in a loop), each triggering an SSE broadcast and re-render. Meanwhile, the server's auto-transition logic in `update.go` already cascades status changes to children — so children were being double-updated.\n\n**Fix in `web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx`:**\n- Removed child status update loops from both the group-drop path (line 392) and the indicator-drop path (line 449)\n- Only the parent's update is sent via `addDraft`; server auto-transitions handle children atomically\n- Removed `batchIds` parameter from `performDrop` (no longer needed for updates)\n- `dragBatchRef` and `getDragGroup` retained for the visual drag overlay (highlighting batch members)"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T07:47:53.638416845Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-b1a394","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T07:47:53.681829611Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-a5a8f1","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T07:50:14.904013827Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-b92fb0","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T08:05:33.734930247Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-b92fb0","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-1fcb7739-56f3-4c77-8fe9-e522d277ee00","text":"## Summary\n\nMade `sort_order` globally consistent across status transitions.\n\n### Root cause\n`backfillSortOrder()` in `internal/beats/projection.go` grouped issues by status and assigned fractional-indexing keys per-group. This meant keys were only meaningful within a status group and were destroyed on status transitions.\n\n### Changes\n\n**Backend — `internal/beats/projection.go`:**\n- Rewrote `backfillSortOrder()` to find the global max `sort_order` across ALL issues and assign keys to unkeyed issues after that global max, in creation-time order. No more per-status grouping.\n\n**Frontend — `web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx`:**\n- Group drop path (dragging onto a status header): now sends only `{ status }`, preserving the existing `sort_order`. The issue's globally-valid key stays intact.\n\n**Frontend — `web/src/components/Board/Board.tsx`:**\n- Cross-column header drops: early return sends only `{ status }`, preserving `sort_order`.\n- Same-column reorder and card-to-card drops: unchanged — neighbor-based key computation works correctly with globally unique keys.\n\n**Tests — `internal/beats/projection_test.go` (new):**\n- `TestBackfillSortOrderGlobal` — unkeyed issues across statuses get globally increasing keys\n- `TestBackfillSortOrderPreservesExisting` — pre-assigned keys unchanged; new keys \u003e global max\n- `TestBackfillSortOrderMixedStatuses` — keyed + unkeyed across statuses\n- `TestBackfillSortOrderEmpty` — empty map, no panic\n- `TestBackfillSortOrderAllKeyed` — all keyed, no changes\n\n### Not changed\n- `sort.ts` (`computeAppendKey` already uses global max)\n- `useBacklogRows.ts` (display concern, still groups by status)\n- `update.go` (auto-transitions only set status, not sort_order — correct)\n- Event model, API responses"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T08:07:46.959932788Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
