{"id":"beats-529e01","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-5fcb5cad-2b65-4b60-9a18-a908509d5b5f","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented a two-layer projection cache in `Server` that avoids re-reading `.beats/issues.db` from disk and re-projecting all events on every API call.\n\n### What changed\n\n**`internal/server/server.go`**\n- Added cache fields to `Server` struct: `cachedEvents`, `cachedIssues`, `lastDBModTime`, `lastDBSize`, `dbExists`, `pendingGen`, `cacheGen`\n- `GetProjectedIssues()` now uses double-checked locking (RLock fast path, Lock slow path). On cache hit: one `os.Stat` (~1μs) + pointer return. On cache miss: disk read + projection, then cached.\n- Added `GetAllEvents()` — same caching for handlers that need raw events (activity feed, cycle progress, issue history)\n- Added `statDB()`, `dbStale()`, `refreshEventsLocked()` helpers\n- `AddPendingEvent()` / `DiscardPending()` / `SaveAndSync()` increment `pendingGen` to invalidate the projection cache\n\n**`internal/server/handlers.go`**\n- `handleActivity`, `handleCycleProgress`, `handleGetIssueHistory` now use `s.GetAllEvents()` instead of calling `storage.ReadEvents()` + manually appending pending events\n\n**`internal/server/cache_test.go`** — 10 new tests covering:\n- Cache hit on repeat calls (pointer identity)\n- Invalidation on file change (mtime/size detection)\n- Invalidation on pending event add/discard\n- `GetAllEvents` caching and pending inclusion\n- DB deletion detection\n- Empty DB caching\n- `SaveAndSync` invalidation\n- External write detection (simulating CLI/MCP writes)\n\n### Design rationale\n\n- **Mtime + size check** is the universal invalidation signal for disk changes — no explicit invalidation needed after `handleDraft`, `handleStartWork`, `handleMergeIssue`, etc. The `os.Stat` call costs ~1μs, negligible vs the avoided disk read + O(n) projection.\n- **`pendingGen` / `cacheGen` counters** track pending buffer changes independently of disk state, so adding/discarding pending events triggers reprojection without touching the events cache.\n- **No file watcher** — the stat-on-read approach is simpler, has zero background goroutines, and catches external writes on the next API call."},"created_at":"2026-06-15T09:45:02.317995228Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-7f6ca6","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-928f2a50-030d-43e2-9b18-f83dfca0bcfa","text":"Resolved as a side effect of beats-529e01 (projection caching). The DnD lag was caused by SSE-triggered refetches calling `GetProjectedIssues()`, which re-read the entire JSONL file and replayed all events on every API call. With the cached projection, those refetches return in ~1μs (stat check + pointer return), eliminating the I/O stall that was blocking the drag loop."},"created_at":"2026-06-15T09:47:23.706151453Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
