{"id":"beats-0a9e5b","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-696a67ec-c871-4613-8750-b17653486ae2","text":"## Summary\n\nConsolidated per-user state into a single `~/.config/beats/user.yaml`, replacing `credentials.yaml`.\n\n- `internal/config/remote.go`:\n  - `Credentials` struct → `UserConfig` (now documented as the single file for all per-user state)\n  - `ServerCredential` extended with `LastRead string` (`yaml:\"last_read,omitempty\"`) per the target schema\n  - `credentialsPath()` → `userConfigPath()`, returning `user.yaml` (still honors `BEATS_CONFIG_DIR`)\n  - `LoadCredentials()`/`SaveCredentials()` → `LoadUserConfig()`/`SaveUserConfig()`\n  - `SaveServerCredential` now **merges** into the existing entry instead of overwriting it, so per-user state (e.g. `last_read`) survives a token refresh on re-login\n  - File permissions remain `0600`\n- Callers updated: `cmd/beats/logout.go` (`LoadUserConfig`), comment fixes in `cmd/beats/login.go` and `internal/config/config.go`\n- Tests (`internal/config/remote_test.go`): permission check now stats `user.yaml`; added `TestSaveServerCredential_PreservesLastRead` covering the merge behavior\n\n## Rationale\n\nThe merge-on-save change was necessary once `ServerCredential` started carrying non-credential state: the old `SaveServerCredential` constructed a fresh struct, which would have silently wiped `last_read` every time a user re-authenticated. Adding the `LastRead` field now (without read/write logic) lands the schema so the inbox work in `beats-7cd82d` can build on it directly.\n\n## Verification\n\n- No references to `credentials.yaml` or the old symbols remain anywhere in the codebase\n- `go build ./...` clean; `go test ./...` all pass\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- ✅ `beats login` writes tokens to `~/.config/beats/user.yaml`\n- ✅ `BEATS_CONFIG_DIR` override still respected\n- ✅ File permissions remain `0600`\n- ✅ No references to `credentials.yaml` remain\n\n## For the next agent\n\n`ServerCredential.LastRead` is wired into the struct/serialization but has no inbox read/write logic yet — that is `beats-7cd82d`."},"created_at":"2026-06-15T11:32:45.134929354Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
