{"id":"beats-e4397a","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\nCreate a comprehensive README.md with install instructions, quickstart guide, and feature overview. This is the first thing users see — it needs to get them from zero to a working beats project in under 2 minutes.\n\n## Sections needed\n\n- **What is beats** — one-paragraph pitch\n- **Install** — binary download, `go install`, homebrew (if applicable), Docker\n- **Quickstart** — `beats init`, `beats add`, `beats board`, screenshot\n- **CLI reference** — summary table of commands\n- **Web UI** — `beats board` launches it, what it looks like\n- **Distributed mode** — `beats serve`, `beats login`, remote setup\n- **Configuration** — `.beats/config.yaml` reference (prefix, cycles, labels, permissions, automations)\n- **MCP integration** — how to use beats with AI agents\n- **Contributing** — `make build`, `make test`, project structure","estimate":3,"labels":["improvement"],"status":"PLANNED","title":"README and install documentation"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T18:39:39.818631401Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-6581f4","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\nToast notifications in the WebUI are too generic (\"Updated\", \"Issue created\") and visually easy to miss. Error toasts are especially problematic — a failed save or API error should be unmissable, not a fleeting gray blip.\n\n## Problems\n\n1. **Generic messages** — \"Updated\" doesn't tell you what happened. Should be \"Status changed to DOING\" or \"Assigned to Alice\".\n2. **Error visibility** — errors use the same toast style as success. A failed save should be red, persistent, and actionable (\"Save failed — retry?\").\n3. **Duration** — success toasts disappear too quickly; error toasts should persist until dismissed.\n\n## Design\n\n### Success toasts\n- Specific messages derived from the action: \"Status changed to DOING\", \"Comment added\", \"Issue created: beats-abc123\", \"Merged via squash\"\n- Brief duration (2-3s), subtle style\n\n### Error toasts\n- Red/error color, persistent until dismissed (click to close)\n- Include the error detail: \"Save failed: server unreachable\" not just \"Error\"\n- Action button where applicable: \"Retry\" for transient failures\n\n### Where to change\n- `web/src/components/ui/Toast.tsx` — add variant support (success/error/warning)\n- Every `showToast()` call site in App.tsx, Backlog.tsx, Board.tsx, IssueDetail, etc. — replace generic messages with specific ones\n- API error catches — surface the error message in the toast","estimate":3,"labels":["improvement","WebApp"],"status":"PLANNED","title":"Actionable toast messages with error visibility"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T18:39:54.147923963Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-0674b9","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\nAudit all user-facing error messages across CLI and WebUI for clarity and actionability. Raw Go errors should never leak to users. Every error should tell the user what went wrong and what to do about it.\n\n## Scope\n\n### CLI\n- Commands that shell out to git — wrap git failures with context (\"failed to create branch: git returned ...\")\n- Config parsing errors — point to the specific field and valid values\n- Network errors in distributed mode — \"cannot reach server at X, check beats serve is running\"\n- Migration errors — clear message + \"your data has not been modified\" safety assurance\n\n### WebUI / API\n- 4xx responses — structured JSON errors with human-readable messages\n- 5xx responses — don't expose stack traces or internal paths\n- Auth failures — distinguish expired token vs missing token vs wrong key\n\n### Patterns to fix\n- `fmt.Errorf(\"error: %w\", err)` — redundant \"error:\" prefix\n- Raw `err.Error()` passed to `respondError` — may contain internal paths\n- Missing context: \"not found\" without saying what wasn't found","estimate":3,"labels":["improvement"],"status":"PLANNED","title":"Error messages audit — user-facing clarity"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T18:40:06.541478114Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
