{"id":"beats-0674b9","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@nicbet-wsl.local\u003e"},"created_at":"2026-06-16T06:20:35.638891135Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-0674b9","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-cb0128e4-c218-4bf2-948b-f490dd8ff684","text":"## Summary\n\nAudited and fixed user-facing error messages across CLI and WebUI. All changes pass `make build` and `make test`.\n\n### HTTP handlers (`internal/server/handlers.go`) — 20 fixes\n- Replaced all raw `err.Error()` in `respondError` 500 calls with descriptive, user-safe messages (e.g. `\"failed to load issues\"`, `\"failed to merge issue %s\"`)\n- Added entity IDs where helpful: `\"issue %s not found\"`, `\"failed to add label %q\"`, `\"failed to update issue %s\"`\n- Replaced generic `\"Invalid request\"` / `\"invalid request\"` with `\"invalid JSON in request body\"` (5 call sites)\n- Replaced `\"Error saving: %v\"` format strings with operation-specific messages (create/update/comment/delete/save)\n- Fixed `\"invalid since parameter: \"+err.Error()` → explains expected RFC3339 format\n- Fixed `\"failed to update read cursor: \"+err.Error()` → drops raw error\n\n### Auth middleware (`internal/auth/middleware.go`) — 1 fix\n- Token verification error now returns generic `\"invalid or expired token\"` instead of raw `VerifyToken` errors (which could leak algorithm/encoding details). Distinguishes `\"token expired\"` for UX.\n\n### Metrics handler (`internal/server/metrics.go`) — 1 fix\n- `\"Failed to load issues: %v\"` → `\"failed to load issues\"` (no raw error leak)\n\n### Proxy error handler (`internal/server/router.go`) — 1 fix\n- `\"remote server unreachable: %v\"` → `\"remote server unreachable — check that the server is running and the URL is correct\"` (guidance instead of raw Go error)\n\n### Remote transport (`internal/beats/remote_transport.go`) — 1 fix\n- `decodeJSON` no longer dumps raw server response body. Parses `{\"error\":\"...\"}` envelope for structured errors, falls back to status code only. Removed unused `io` import.\n\n### Migration (`internal/beats/migrate.go`) — 2 fixes\n- `\"v2→v3 migration failed\"` → adds safety assurance: `\"your data has not been modified\"`\n- `\"failed to update config version\"` → clarifies the migration succeeded and a retry will fix it\n\n### Internal error prefix cleanup — 18 fixes across 8 files\nReplaced `\"error \u003cverb\u003eing ...\"` prefix pattern with consistent `\"failed to \u003cverb\u003e ...\"` across:\n- `maintenance.go`, `local_transport.go`, `comment.go`, `delete.go`, `list.go`, `add.go`, `update.go`, `setup.go`\n\n### Intentionally left as-is\n- `handleStartWork` 409 errors: these are user-facing domain messages (e.g. \"issue X is already DONE\") that are clear and actionable by design\n- `http.Error()` in auth middleware for missing/invalid auth header: correctly returns JSON error, separate package from `respondError`\n- SSE endpoint `http.Error()` calls: SSE clients expect text responses, not JSON\n- `panic()` on embedded FS failure in `router.go`: startup invariant, correct to panic"},"created_at":"2026-06-16T06:29:50.169079432Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
