{"id":"beats-918bd8","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-0efc193e-0354-4785-bc23-ab344a32e9ad","text":"## Summary\n\n**Root cause**: `onKeyDown={handleKeyDown}` was attached to both the `\u003cinput\u003e` element and its parent `\u003cdiv\u003e` in `CommandPalette.tsx`. Arrow key events fired on the input, then bubbled to the parent, calling `setSelectedIndex` twice per keypress — each using a functional updater (`i =\u003e i + 1`), so both increments applied.\n\n**Fix**: Removed the duplicate `onKeyDown` from the `\u003cinput\u003e`. The event naturally bubbles to the parent `\u003cdiv\u003e` where it's handled once."},"created_at":"2026-06-16T07:20:13.091035587Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-918bd8","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-16T07:21:24.970360019Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-adb33e","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"The unread count badge currently counts the number of updates, which inflates what we actually do see in the inbox. For example one issue with 5 updates creates one card in the inbox but the badge in the sidebar says \"5\".","labels":["improvement"],"sort_order":"b22","title":"Unread count badge should count issues modified instead of global change events"},"created_at":"2026-06-16T07:23:21.141406975Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-adb33e","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a2l"},"created_at":"2026-06-16T07:23:36.94788679Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-adb33e","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@nicbet-wsl.local\u003e"},"created_at":"2026-06-16T07:26:00.379707903Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-adb33e","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-89a1bc15-7b95-4b31-9039-e5b0596ecf01","text":"## Summary\n\n**Root cause**: `handleInboxStatus` in `internal/server/handlers.go` returned `len(beats.BuildInbox(...))` as the unread count. `BuildInbox` returns one item per event, but the web UI groups events by issue ID — so 5 updates to 1 issue showed a badge of \"5\" instead of \"1\".\n\n**Fix**: Count distinct issue IDs from the inbox items instead of raw item count. Now the sidebar badge matches what the user actually sees in the inbox view."},"created_at":"2026-06-16T07:26:52.33792405Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-adb33e","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-16T07:30:15.976062886Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-10af26","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Inbox redesign — nested event cards, natural sentences, unread count fix","description":"Redesigned the inbox view:\\n\\n- Card header: StatusIcon + bold accent-colored issue ID + title + event count\\n- Nested event cards with expand/collapse — latest event always visible, older behind \\\"K more\\\" toggle\\n- Natural sentence format: \\\"**Alice** started working on this\\\", \\\"**Bob** left a comment\\\"\\n- Event icons colored only for status changes; everything else neutral\\n- Unread badge counts distinct issues instead of raw events\\n- Width aligned to `max-w-4xl` standard\\n- Inverted default avatar colors for dark theme\\n- Removed redundant blue unread dot (tabs handle read/unread separation)","status":"DONE","labels":["improvement"]},"created_at":"2026-06-16T07:44:49.13157969Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-10af26","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"source_id":"beats-10af26","target_id":"beats-adb33e","kind":"relates_to"}]},"created_at":"2026-06-16T07:44:52.897377593Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-78471c","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"sort_order":"a3V"},"created_at":"2026-06-16T07:56:40.576849391Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-be2720","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\\n\\nAudit of keyboard navigation across the Web UI. The backlog and issue detail views have good coverage (J/K nav, S/L/E/P/A shortcuts, number-key status changes). But several views have no keyboard support at all, modals don't trap focus, and there's no way for users to discover available shortcuts.\\n\\n## Release-blocking\\n\\nThese create a broken or frustrating experience for keyboard users:\\n\\n### Focus management in modals\\n- Modals (new issue, merge confirmation) have no focus trap — Tab escapes the modal\\n- No auto-focus on first input when modal opens\\n- No focus restoration when modal closes\\n- Files: `Modal.tsx`, `NewIssueModal.tsx`\\n\\n### Filter menu traps keyboard in backlog\\n- When the filter menu is open (`F` key), all backlog keyboard nav is disabled\\n- Escape doesn't close the filter menu — user must click elsewhere\\n- File: `Backlog.tsx` line 693\\n\\n### Keyboard shortcut discoverability\\n- No help overlay or cheat sheet (`?` key is the convention)\\n- Shortcuts exist but users can't discover them without reading code\\n- Accelerator hints should appear in context menus, popovers, and toolbar buttons\\n\\n## High priority (pre-release polish)\\n\\n### Board view — zero keyboard nav\\n- No arrow key navigation between columns or cards\\n- No Enter to open card detail\\n- No status shortcuts (S/L/E) on focused card\\n- Only dnd-kit's built-in keyboard drag exists\\n- File: `Board.tsx`\\n\\n### Inbox — zero keyboard nav\\n- No J/K or arrow key navigation between issue groups\\n- No Enter to open linked issue\\n- No keyboard shortcut to mark all as read\\n- File: `Inbox.tsx`\\n\\n### Number-key status in context menu submenus\\n- Issue detail supports 1-5 for status changes\\n- Context menu status submenu (right-click on backlog row) doesn't support number selection\\n- Inconsistent: same UI, different keyboard behavior\\n- File: `ContextMenu.tsx`\\n\\n## Nice-to-have (post-release)\\n\\n### Global view switching\\n- Number keys (e.g., `G` then `B` for board, `G` then `I` for inbox) or direct shortcuts\\n- Currently only reachable via command palette\\n\\n### Dashboard keyboard nav\\n- Arrow key navigation through attention items, epics, workload entries\\n- Enter to jump to linked issue\\n\\n### Search focus shortcut\\n- `/` to focus the backlog search input (common convention)\\n- Currently unreachable without mouse or multiple Tab presses\\n\\n### Consistent J/K everywhere\\n- Backlog and issue detail support J/K (vim-style)\\n- Board, inbox, dashboard don't\\n- Should work in any list context\\n\\n## Current coverage matrix\\n\\n| View | Arrow/J/K nav | Shortcuts | Enter to open | Escape to close |\\n|------|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\\n| Command Palette | Yes | — | Yes | Yes |\\n| Backlog | Yes | S/L/E/F/. | Yes | — |\\n| Issue Detail | Yes (prev/next) | S/L/E/P/A/M/1-5/. | — | Yes |\\n| Board | No | No | No | — |\\n| Inbox | No | No | No | — |\\n| Dashboard | No | No | No | — |\\n| Modals | — | Cmd+Enter | — | Yes (no trap) |","estimate":8,"labels":["improvement","epic"],"status":"PLANNED","title":"Keyboard navigation — consistency, discoverability, and gaps"},"created_at":"2026-06-16T08:04:04.504256863Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-a24553","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Problem\\n\\nModals (new issue, merge confirmation) don't trap keyboard focus — Tab escapes the modal into the background. No auto-focus on first input when opening, no focus restoration when closing.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n- Add focus trap to `Modal.tsx` (prevent Tab from escaping)\\n- Auto-focus first focusable element on open\\n- Restore focus to trigger element on close\\n- Apply to `NewIssueModal.tsx`, merge confirmation, and any other modal consumers\\n\\n## Files\\n- `web/src/components/ui/Modal.tsx`\\n- `web/src/components/NewIssueModal/NewIssueModal.tsx`\\n- `web/src/components/IssueDetail/MergeView.tsx`","estimate":2,"labels":["improvement"],"parent_id":"beats-be2720","status":"PLANNED","title":"Focus trap and auto-focus for modals"},"created_at":"2026-06-16T08:05:48.331655383Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-1e720d","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Problem\\n\\nWhen the backlog filter menu is open (via `F` key), all keyboard navigation is disabled and Escape doesn't close it. User must click elsewhere with the mouse — keyboard trap with no exit.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n- Add Escape handler to close filter menu\\n- Restore backlog keyboard nav after filter menu closes\\n\\n## Files\\n- `web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx` (line ~693)\\n- `web/src/components/Backlog/FilterMenu.tsx`","estimate":1,"labels":["bug"],"parent_id":"beats-be2720","status":"PLANNED","title":"Filter menu Escape handling in backlog"},"created_at":"2026-06-16T08:05:51.228202545Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-c57e08","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Problem\\n\\nShortcuts exist but are undiscoverable — users can't find them without reading code.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n- `?` key opens a help overlay listing all keyboard shortcuts\\n- Grouped by context: Global, Backlog, Issue Detail, Board, etc.\\n- Overlay closes on Escape or `?` again\\n- Add accelerator hints to context menus, popovers, and toolbar buttons where applicable\\n\\n## Files\\n- New component: `web/src/components/KeyboardHelp/`\\n- `web/src/App.tsx` (register `?` global shortcut)\\n- Various components for inline hints","estimate":2,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"beats-be2720","status":"PLANNED","title":"Keyboard shortcut help overlay (?)"},"created_at":"2026-06-16T08:05:58.121573701Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-d86e61","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Problem\\n\\nBoard view has zero keyboard navigation — only dnd-kit's built-in keyboard drag exists.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n- Arrow Up/Down (or J/K): navigate cards within a column\\n- Arrow Left/Right: move focus between columns\\n- Enter: open focused card's detail view\\n- S/L/E shortcuts on focused card (same as backlog)\\n- Visual focus indicator on active card\\n\\n## Files\\n- `web/src/components/Board/Board.tsx`\\n- `web/src/components/Board/BoardCard.tsx`","estimate":3,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"beats-be2720","status":"PLANNED","title":"Board view keyboard navigation"},"created_at":"2026-06-16T08:05:58.862942253Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-be2720","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"sort_order":"a2"},"created_at":"2026-06-16T08:05:59.64074837Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-3b16a4","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Inbox keyboard navigation","description":"## Problem\\n\\nInbox has no keyboard support at all.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n- Arrow Up/Down (or J/K): navigate between issue groups\\n- Enter: open the linked issue\\n- Visual focus indicator on active group\\n- Keyboard shortcut to mark all as read\\n\\n## Files\\n- `web/src/components/Inbox/Inbox.tsx`","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"beats-be2720","estimate":2,"labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-06-16T08:06:00.762048476Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-9c933d","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Number-key status selection in context menu","description":"## Problem\\n\\nIssue detail supports 1-5 for quick status changes, but the context menu's status submenu (right-click on backlog row) doesn't. Same UI, different keyboard behavior.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n- Add 1-5 number key handlers in the status submenu of `ContextMenu.tsx`\\n- Match the ordering used in issue detail: 1=Backlog, 2=Planned, 3=Doing, 4=Blocked, 5=Done\\n\\n## Files\\n- `web/src/components/ui/ContextMenu.tsx`","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"beats-be2720","estimate":1,"labels":["improvement"]},"created_at":"2026-06-16T08:06:04.081244186Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-0f271b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Global view switching shortcuts","description":"## Problem\\n\\nSwitching between views (backlog, board, inbox, dashboard) requires the command palette or mouse clicks on the sidebar.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n- `G` then `B`: switch to Backlog (issues)\\n- `G` then `O`: switch to Board\\n- `G` then `D`: switch to Dashboard\\n- `G` then `I`: switch to Inbox\\n- `G` then `E`: switch to Dependencies\\n- Two-key chord: `G` sets a pending state (with brief timeout), second key completes the nav\\n- Show `G` chord hint in sidebar nav items\\n\\n## Files\\n- `web/src/App.tsx` (global handler)\\n- `web/src/components/Layout/Layout.tsx` (sidebar hints)","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"beats-be2720","estimate":2,"labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-06-16T08:06:09.294644767Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-fc2d80","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"/ shortcut to focus backlog search","description":"## Problem\\n\\nBacklog search input is unreachable without mouse or many Tab presses.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n- `/` key focuses the search input when in backlog view (common convention: GitHub, Slack, etc.)\\n- Escape from search returns focus to the issue list\\n- Ensure `/` doesn't fire when already in an editable target\\n\\n## Files\\n- `web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx`","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"beats-be2720","estimate":1,"labels":["improvement"]},"created_at":"2026-06-16T08:06:12.108784117Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
