{"id":"beats-f6c313","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-5de4f3a3-dff5-4ca0-ad7d-5d55af9142a3","text":"## Summary\n\nReduced initial JS bundle from 476KB gzip (single chunk) to 95KB gzip with code splitting and manual vendor chunks.\n\n### Code splitting via lazy routes\nLazy-loaded 7 views with `React.lazy()`: Dashboard, Board, Dependencies, Labels, Cycles, Inbox, IssueDetail. Each becomes its own chunk, loaded on demand. Backlog stays in the main bundle (most common landing view).\n\n### Manual vendor chunks\nSplit heavy dependencies into stable, independently cacheable chunks:\n- `vendor-charts` (recharts): 334KB / 101KB gz — only loaded with Dashboard\n- `vendor-editor` (tiptap): 505KB / 175KB gz — only loaded when editing descriptions\n- `vendor-markdown` (react-markdown + remark): 157KB / 48KB gz — loaded with Inbox/IssueDetail\n- `vendor-dnd` (@dnd-kit): 61KB / 21KB gz — loaded with Backlog/Board\n\n### Results\n\n| Metric | Before | After |\n|--------|--------|-------|\n| Initial load (gzip) | 476KB | 95KB |\n| Chunks | 1 | 13 |\n| Largest vendor (gzip) | — | 175KB (editor, on demand) |\n\n### Files changed\n- `web/vite.config.ts` — `manualChunks` configuration\n- `web/src/App.tsx` — `React.lazy()` imports, `Suspense` wrapper"},"created_at":"2026-06-16T15:04:15.198531817Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
